ired_providers — only used in child modules","tree":{"sha":"afb69217a6728e4d6c816b4f0dfbc3d9360620b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/git/trees/afb69217a6728e4d6c816b4f0dfbc3d9360620b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/git/commits/7d67a4e29b0f8c26585f610c760e89964ca41fe6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6948843?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shanepreater","id":6948843,"login":"shanepreater","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDg4NDM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commit/7d67a4e29b0f8c26585f610c760e89964ca41fe6","node_id":"C_kwDOSrf_edoAKDdkNjdhNGUyOWIwZjhjMjY1ODVmNjEwYzc2MGU4OTk2NGNhNDFmZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commit/5c0d810ab6f207a847dbf273260b492458d72682","sha":"5c0d810ab6f207a847dbf273260b492458d72682","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/5c0d810ab6f207a847dbf273260b492458d72682"}],"sha":"7d67a4e29b0f8c26585f610c760e89964ca41fe6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/7d67a4e29b0f8c26585f610c760e89964ca41fe6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6948843?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shanepreater","id":6948843,"login":"shanepreater","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDg4NDM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/5c0d810ab6f207a847dbf273260b492458d72682/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T13:09:53Z","email":"shane@argodevops.co.uk","name":"Shane P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T13:09:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(deployment): UAT environment fixes — ACA URLs, Keycloak realm import, production script (#44)\n\n* fix(deployment): fix uat-stop max-replicas and add app existence guards\n\nuat-stop.sh set --max-replicas 0, which ACA rejects (valid range\n1–1000). Scale-to-zero requires min=0 with max>=1; fixed to max=1.\n\nBoth uat-start.sh and uat-stop.sh would hard-fail via set -euo pipefail\nwhen a container app doesn''t exist yet (e.g. before Terraform apply).\nAdded an existence check before each az containerapp update so missing\napps are skipped with a clear message instead of aborting the script.\n\n* feat(deployment): add production deployment script and BOM version\n\ndeploy-production.sh tags latest main as production_<BOM_version>,\npushes the tag, and fires the Deploy workflow via workflow_dispatch.\nGuards against re-tagging an already-released version.\n\nAdded platform=0.1.0 to root VERSION as the overall BOM release\nversion that the script reads for the tag name.\n\n* fix(terraform): derive ACA URLs from environment default_domain\n\nVNet-integrated Container App environments get a random FQDN hash\n(e.g. happyocean-c0a86abb.uksouth.azurecontainerapps.io) rather than\na workspace-slug-based domain. Hardcoded workspace_slug URLs caused\nKC_HOSTNAME, NEXTAUTH_URL, and all inter-service Keycloak URLs to\npoint at non-existent hostnames, breaking the SSO login flow.\n\nReplaced the three workspace_slug patterns in the container-apps\nmodule locals with references to azurerm_container_app_environment\n.main.default_domain, which Terraform resolves after the environment\nis created and before the container apps are planned.\n\n* feat(terraform): Keycloak realm import via Azure Files + decouple production CI\n\n- Provision Azure Storage Account + File Share for Keycloak realm import;\n  render spyder realm JSON inline via jsonencode (clients with correct ACA\n  redirect URIs derived from default_domain, roles, seed users), upload as\n  azurerm_storage_share_file, mount into Keycloak at /opt/keycloak/data/import,\n  pass --import-realm so the realm is auto-imported on first Keycloak boot.\n  Eliminates manual Keycloak configuration after every Terraform replace.\n- Add hashicorp/local ~> 2.5 provider to modules/container-apps and root;\n  update .terraform.lock.hcl; add mock_provider \"local\" to unit test file;\n  add .gitignore for the rendered spyder-realm.json local file.\n- Remove automated plan-production CI job: waiting for TFC approval held the\n  workflow concurrency group open (cancel-in-progress: false), blocking\n  subsequent UAT workflow_run triggers. Production deployments are now manual\n  via scripts/deploy-production.sh + TFC UI. Update docs/cicd.md accordingly.\n\n* fix(terraform): address Infracost FinOps policy violations on Keycloak storage account\n\n- Set public_network_access_enabled=false + deny-by-default network_rules\n  (bypass AzureServices, allow container_apps subnet via VNet service endpoint)\n- Add Microsoft.Storage service endpoint to container_apps subnet in networking\n  module so the ACA environment can still mount the Azure Files share\n- Add blob_properties.last_access_time_enabled=true and\n  azurerm_storage_management_policy to satisfy lifecycle policy check\n- Add Environment (Prod/Stage/Dev) and Service tags to common_tags so all\n  resources satisfy the Infracost FinOps tagging policy on future PRs\n\n* fix(ci): add explicit PR trigger types to terraform workflow + fix infracost violations\n\n- Add types: [opened, synchronize, reopened] to terraform.yml pull_request\n  trigger (matches ci.yml pattern); the missing explicit types likely prevented\n  the workflow from firing on the feature/uat-deployment PR\n- Move trailing comment out of the jobs: block to top-level to avoid any\n  YAML parser edge cases\n- PostgreSQL: change UAT backup_retention_days to 7 (policy requires 7 for\n  non-production; was 14); add auto_grow_enabled=true to all environments\n- Add infracost usage files (UAT + production) with sensible estimates for\n  log analytics ingestion, container registry storage, keycloak config storage,\n  and PostgreSQL backup overhead; wire them into infracost configuration.yml\n- Add production project to infracost configuration (workspaces/production.tfvars)\n  so production costs appear in PR diffs alongside UAT\n\n* fix(ci): restore plan-production as plan_only to avoid concurrency deadlock\n\nThe previous plan-production job created a non-speculative TFC run and waited\nfor human approval, which held the GitHub Actions workflow open indefinitely.\nWith cancel-in-progress: false this blocked all subsequent UAT workflow_run\ntriggers from the same concurrency group.\n\nFix: use plan_only: true so TFC completes the run immediately after planning\nwith no approval gate. The plan output is still visible in the Actions log for\nreview before a manual apply via scripts/deploy-production.sh.","tree":{"sha":"decd38778afd331bc7646a367f4615df78bdd9c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/git/trees/decd38778afd331bc7646a367f4615df78bdd9c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/git/commits/5c0d810ab6f207a847dbf273260b492458d72682","verification":{"payload":"tree decd38778afd331bc7646a367f4615df78bdd9c7\nparent bf79826374862700c20c6e3ba801cdeaa5f3c7c5\nauthor Shane P <shane@argodevops.co.uk> 1779800993 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779800993 +0100\n\nfeat(deployment): UAT environment fixes — ACA URLs, Keycloak realm import, production script (#44)\n\n* fix(deployment): fix uat-stop max-replicas and add app existence guards\n\nuat-stop.sh set --max-replicas 0, which ACA rejects (valid range\n1–1000). Scale-to-zero requires min=0 with max>=1; fixed to max=1.\n\nBoth uat-start.sh and uat-stop.sh would hard-fail via set -euo pipefail\nwhen a container app doesn''t exist yet (e.g. before Terraform apply).\nAdded an existence check before each az containerapp update so missing\napps are skipped with a clear message instead of aborting the script.\n\n* feat(deployment): add production deployment script and BOM version\n\ndeploy-production.sh tags latest main as production_<BOM_version>,\npushes the tag, and fires the Deploy workflow via workflow_dispatch.\nGuards against re-tagging an already-released version.\n\nAdded platform=0.1.0 to root VERSION as the overall BOM release\nversion that the script reads for the tag name.\n\n* fix(terraform): derive ACA URLs from environment default_domain\n\nVNet-integrated Container App environments get a random FQDN hash\n(e.g. happyocean-c0a86abb.uksouth.azurecontainerapps.io) rather than\na workspace-slug-based domain. Hardcoded workspace_slug URLs caused\nKC_HOSTNAME, NEXTAUTH_URL, and all inter-service Keycloak URLs to\npoint at non-existent hostnames, breaking the SSO login flow.\n\nReplaced the three workspace_slug patterns in the container-apps\nmodule locals with references to azurerm_container_app_environment\n.main.default_domain, which Terraform resolves after the environment\nis created and before the container apps are planned.\n\n* feat(terraform): Keycloak realm import via Azure Files + decouple production CI\n\n- Provision Azure Storage Account + File Share for Keycloak realm import;\n  render spyder realm JSON inline via jsonencode (clients with correct ACA\n  redirect URIs derived from default_domain, roles, seed users), upload as\n  azurerm_storage_share_file, mount into Keycloak at /opt/keycloak/data/import,\n  pass --import-realm so the realm is auto-imported on first Keycloak boot.\n  Eliminates manual Keycloak configuration after every Terraform replace.\n- Add hashicorp/local ~> 2.5 provider to modules/container-apps and root;\n  update .terraform.lock.hcl; add mock_provider \"local\" to unit test file;\n  add .gitignore for the rendered spyder-realm.json local file.\n- Remove automated plan-production CI job: waiting for TFC approval held the\n  workflow concurrency group open (cancel-in-progress: false), blocking\n  subsequent UAT workflow_run triggers. Production deployments are now manual\n  via scripts/deploy-production.sh + TFC UI. Update docs/cicd.md accordingly.\n\n* fix(terraform): address Infracost FinOps policy violations on Keycloak storage account\n\n- Set public_network_access_enabled=false + deny-by-default network_rules\n  (bypass AzureServices, allow container_apps subnet via VNet service endpoint)\n- Add Microsoft.Storage service endpoint to container_apps subnet in networking\n  module so the ACA environment can still mount the Azure Files share\n- Add blob_properties.last_access_time_enabled=true and\n  azurerm_storage_management_policy to satisfy lifecycle policy check\n- Add Environment (Prod/Stage/Dev) and Service tags to common_tags so all\n  resources satisfy the Infracost FinOps tagging policy on future PRs\n\n* fix(ci): add explicit PR trigger types to terraform workflow + fix infracost violations\n\n- Add types: [opened, synchronize, reopened] to terraform.yml pull_request\n  trigger (matches ci.yml pattern); the missing explicit types likely prevented\n  the workflow from firing on the feature/uat-deployment PR\n- Move trailing comment out of the jobs: block to top-level to avoid any\n  YAML parser edge cases\n- PostgreSQL: change UAT backup_retention_days to 7 (policy requires 7 for\n  non-production; was 14); add auto_grow_enabled=true to all environments\n- Add infracost usage files (UAT + production) with sensible estimates for\n  log analytics ingestion, container registry storage, keycloak config storage,\n  and PostgreSQL backup overhead; wire them into infracost configuration.yml\n- Add production project to infracost configuration (workspaces/production.tfvars)\n  so production costs appear in PR diffs alongside UAT\n\n* fix(ci): restore plan-production as plan_only to avoid concurrency deadlock\n\nThe previous plan-production job created a non-speculative TFC run and waited\nfor human approval, which held the GitHub Actions workflow open indefinitely.\nWith cancel-in-progress: false this blocked all subsequent UAT workflow_run\ntriggers from the same concurrency group.\n\nFix: use plan_only: true so TFC completes the run immediately after planning\nwith no approval gate. The plan output is still visible in the Actions log for\nreview before a manual apply via scripts/deploy-production.sh.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqFZuhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/TMQAEYLpYXM34cMvIXFVzm3E+rK\nGJ76if2qVvXL0H6E7mjC9Vqr6/3EWZRNUJJLAaCInv+kK7sfFBpOU94aIN674Dmf\n6ecZb08W66+2tM242y12lOk8r/tr