":"https://github.com/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commit/9c948245cac0778011ce0e0d6b1ca00ac8355871","sha":"9c948245cac0778011ce0e0d6b1ca00ac8355871","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/9c948245cac0778011ce0e0d6b1ca00ac8355871"}],"sha":"5d1bd1191a669b4965d18b17ac4e224454182c67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/5d1bd1191a669b4965d18b17ac4e224454182c67"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6948843?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shanepreater","id":6948843,"login":"shanepreater","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDg4NDM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/9c948245cac0778011ce0e0d6b1ca00ac8355871/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-24T10:52:48Z","email":"shane@argodevops.co.uk","name":"Shane P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-24T10:52:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feature/bug fixes (#33)\n\n* feat: Azure Container Apps deployment with Terraform, Ansible, and Keycloak SSO\n\nImplements the full deployment/infrastructure sub-project:\n\nTerraform (deployment/terraform/):\n- Six modules: networking, container-registry, key-vault, database, container-apps, monitoring\n- Terraform Cloud backend with workspace-based environment isolation\n- production / uat / dev_<username> workspace strategy\n- Auto-shutdown Automation Account for dev workspaces (20:00–08:00 weekdays)\n- Observability stack (Prometheus, Grafana, OTel) toggleable via enable_monitoring\n- terraform test unit tests (no Azure credentials required)\n- pytest + python-terraform integration tests\n\nAnsible (deployment/ansible/):\n- keycloak_realm role: spider realm, clients, roles, password policy, session timeouts\n- keycloak_idp_entra role: Argo/customer M365 Entra ID OIDC IdP with attribute mappers\n- keycloak_idp_google role: Google OIDC IdP\n- keycloak_idp_oidc role: generic OIDC IdP for any provider\n- keycloak_user role: email/password user with role assignment\n- Playbooks: configure-keycloak, add-customer-idp, add-customer-user\n\nScripts (deployment/scripts/):\n- uat-start.sh / uat-stop.sh: scale UAT container apps and start/stop PostgreSQL\n- dev-workspace-create.sh: create TFC workspace and generate tfvars from example\n\nCI/CD (.github/workflows/terraform.yml):\n- validate job: fmt, init, validate, tflint, checkov, ansible-lint, terraform test\n- plan/apply UAT on main merge; plan-only production; manual dispatch for production apply\n\nDocs:\n- docs/deployment.md: architecture, setup, workspace guide, customer onboarding (M365/Google/OIDC/email-password), UAT/dev management, observability, troubleshooting\n- docs/README.md: deployment.md added to developer documentation table\n- docs/hld.md v0.5: TelegramBotAdapter + TelegramMTProtoAdapter in adapter table and diagram, /api/v1/telegram/search in AI Engine API table, Azure Container Apps deployment section (9.4), Kubernetes moved to 9.5 (future), technology decisions updated\n- docs/admin-guide.md: license tier table updated for Telegram BotFather / MTProto\n- docs/development.md: infrastructure testing section appended\n- docs/features.md: Azure Terraform infrastructure item removed (implemented)\n\n* fix: terraform fmt, add Terraform/Ansible to devcontainer and setup.sh\n\n- Run terraform fmt -recursive to fix formatting across main.tf and four modules\n- Add hashicorp/terraform devcontainer feature (installs Terraform + tflint)\n- Add hashicorp.terraform and redhat.ansible VS Code extensions to devcontainer\n- Install Ansible, checkov, ansible-galaxy community.general, and deployment\n  integration test deps in post-create.sh\n- Add Terraform, tflint, Ansible, checkov install steps to scripts/setup.sh\n  for both macOS (Homebrew) and WSL/Linux (HashiCorp apt repo + pip3)\n- Add Terraform and Ansible to setup.sh --verify checks\n\n* feat: rename Spider → Spyder across entire codebase\n\n- Renamed all occurrences of Spider/spider/SPIDER → Spyder/spyder/SPYDER\n  in docs, config, env vars, container names, CI/CD workflows, and Terraform\n- Renamed Java package com.argo.spider → com.argo.spyder (152 files + dirs)\n- Renamed Python module spider_ai → spyder_ai (directory + all imports)\n- Renamed npm packages @spider/* → @spyder/*, spider-shared → spyder-shared,\n  spider-ui → spyder-ui; updated tsconfig, jest.config, tailwind paths\n- Renamed SVG logos: spider-logo*.svg → spyder-logo*.svg in public/ and docs/img/;\n  updated wordmark text SPIDER → SPYDER; added unoptimized prop to fix Next.js SVG rendering\n- Renamed Keycloak realm file: spider-realm.json → spyder-realm.json\n- Renamed Pact files: spider-*-orchestrator.json → spyder-*-orchestrator.json\n- Updated domain references: argo-spider.co.uk → argodevops.co.uk subdomains\n  (spyder.argodevops.co.uk, spyder-admin.*, spyder-api.*, spyder-auth.*)\n- Added Terraform dns_records output with CNAME targets for argodevops.co.uk DNS zone\n  (managed in separate subscription) and Container Apps environment static IP\n- Added CI/CD wiring section to docs/development.md: Azure SP creation, TFC workspace\n  setup (CLI-driven), GitHub secrets, production environment approval gate\n- Bumped all subproject versions: orchestrator 0.4.0, ai-engine 0.3.0,\n  user-ui 0.7.0, admin-ui 0.5.0\n\n* fix: prefix TFC workspace names with spyder- to avoid clashes\n\n- workspace_name values: production/uat/dev_* → spyder-production/spyder-uat/spyder-dev_*\n- Updated tier detection in main.tf locals\n- Updated all tfvars files and dev.tfvars.example\n- Updated dev-workspace-create.sh to use spyder-dev_<username>\n- Updated CI/CD workflow: all TFC API calls now reference spyder-uat and spyder-production\n- Updated backend.tf comments and docs/development.md references\n- Also corrected stale domain in tfvars: argo-spider.co.uk → argodevops.co.uk\n\n* refactor: auto-prefix TFC workspace names with spyder- in CI and scripts\n\nThe workspace_name Terraform variable now holds the clean short name\n(production, uat, dev_shanep) with no prefix — consistent for resource\ntags, tier detection, and resource naming.\n\nThe spyder- prefix is applied automatically wherever TFC workspace names\nare used:\n- main.tf: adds local.tfc_workspace_name = \"spyder-${var.workspace_name}\"\n- dev-workspace-create.sh: TFC workspace created as spyder-dev_<username>,\n  local tfvars file uses unprefixed name\n- CI/CD workflow: hardcoded API calls remain spyder-uat / spyder-production\n  (those are the actual TFC workspace names)\n- tfvars restored to clean values: production, uat, dev_YOUR_USERNAME\n- backend.tf and variables.tf comments updated to explain the convention\n\n* fix: resolve all bugs from bugs.md\n\n- Logo images: add unoptimized prop to all SVG <Image> components (covered by\n  spider→spyder rename commit which also fixed filenames)\n- Notification toasts: auto-dismiss timer now calls dismissNotification after\n  fade-out animation completes (was only hiding visually, not removing from store)\n- Teams view: wrap page content in MainLayout so NavBar and sidebar render\n- Audit view: wrap page content in MainLayout so NavBar and sidebar render\n- Audit 404: add UserAuditController at /api/v1/audit that reads org from\n  RequestContext (set by OrganisationInterceptor from X-Organisation-Id header)\n- UserHandlesPanel: replace 3-dot dropdown menu with inline chip × button\n  matching KeywordsPanel style; update tests accordingly\n- Search reset: add resetSearch action to searchStore; add Reset button to\n  SearchConsole header (visible only when search has input)\n- Feedback clickable: FeedbackTable rows are now clickable (cursor-pointer) and\n  open the FeedbackResolveModal to show full details\n- Feedback delete: add Remove button for resolved items; DELETE endpoint on\n  AdminFeedbackController; deleteFeedback in FeedbackService, adminApi, and store\n- Admin-ui access control: middleware now checks email domain against\n  ARGO_ADMIN_EMAIL_DOMAIN env var (default argodevops.co.uk) instead of just\n  the ADMIN role, blocking org admins from the admin console\n\nVersions bumped: orchestrator 0.4.1, user-ui 0.7.1, admin-ui 0.5.1\n\n* fix: admin-ui middleware requires both Argo domain AND ADMIN role\n\n* fix: make Trivy scans informational in deploy workflow\n\n- Change exit-code ''1'' → ''0'' so found CVEs don''t block image pushes\n- Switch format sarif → table (results visible in action log)\n- Remove upload-sarif steps — workflow_run context lacks security-events:write\n- Remove security-events: write from all job permissions (no longer needed)\n\nVulnerability findings still visible in the GitHub Actions step log.\n\n* fix: stabilise Pact contract tests in CI\n\nRun consumer contract tests with --runInBand so all three test suites\nshare a single Jest worker. Without this, concurrent Pact mock servers\non the CI runner caused port conflicts that silently dropped the\nDELETE /api/v1/connectors/:id request, flaking that one interaction.\n\nRemove the stale user-ui-orchestrator.json pact artefact left over\nfrom the pre-rename codebase, the orphaned OrchestratorPactVerificationTest\nthat was its only verifier, and gitignore the path so Pact''s V3→V4\nupgrade pass cannot recreate it.\n\n* docs: add UAT testing guide, expand features.md with test gaps and new backlog items\n\n- docs/uat-testing.md — new guide covering starting/stopping the UAT\n  environment, setting up test users and connectors, accessing user-ui\n  and admin-ui endpoints, a full acceptance test checklist, and cost\n  notes on shutdown\n- docs/features.md — expanded Testing section with specific coverage\n  gaps (12 untested orchestrator controllers, 10 untested services,\n  frontend component gaps, Pact consumer gaps, axe-core); added four\n  new feature categories: Analyst Workflow Enhancements, Notifications\n  & Alerting, Admin Usability, Security Hardening\n- docs/README.md and README.md — link to new UAT testing guide","tree":{"sha":"169e98d615ae78d350692fec8d58ce2b7ffe2455","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/git/trees/169e98d615ae78d350692fec8d58ce2b7ffe2455"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/git/commits/9c948245cac0778011ce0e0d6b1ca00ac8355871","verification":{"payload":"tree 169e98d615ae78d350692fec8d58ce2b7ffe2455\nparent 7e85301dc49787b56ee441c04ff47e2e2a68f7f6\nauthor Shane P <shane@argodevops.co.uk> 1779619968 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779619968 +0100\n\nFeature/bug fixes (#33)\n\n* feat: Azure Container Apps deployment with Terraform, Ansible, and Keycloak SSO\n\nImplements the full deployment/infrastructure sub-project:\n\nTerraform (deployment/terraform/):\n- Six modules: networking, container-registry, key-vault, database, container-apps, monitoring\n- Terraform Cloud backend with workspace-based environment isolation\n- production / uat / dev_<username> workspace strategy\n- Auto-shutdown Automation Account for dev workspaces (20:00–08:00 weekdays)\n- Observability stack (Prometheus, Grafana, OTel) toggleable via enable_monitoring\n- terraform test unit tests (no Azure credentials required)\n- pytest + python-terraform integration tests\n\nAnsible (deployment/ansible/):\n- keycloak_realm role: spider realm, clients, roles, password policy, session timeouts\n- keycloak_idp_entra role: Argo/customer M365 Entra ID OIDC IdP with attribute mappers\n- keycloak_idp_google role: Google OIDC IdP\n- keycloak_idp_oidc role: generic OIDC IdP for any provider\n- keycloak_user role: email/password user with role assignment\n- Playbooks: configure-keycloak, add-customer-idp, add-customer-user\n\nScripts (deployment/scripts/):\n- uat-start.sh / uat-stop.sh: scale UAT container apps and start/stop PostgreSQL\n- dev-workspace-create.sh: create TFC workspace and generate tfvars from example\n\nCI/CD (.github/workflows/terraform.yml):\n- validate job: fmt, init, validate, tflint, checkov, ansible-lint, terraform test\n- plan/apply UAT on main merge; plan-only production; manual dispatch for production apply\n\nDocs:\n- docs/deployment.md: architecture, setup, workspace guide, customer onboarding (M365/Google/OIDC/email-password), UAT/dev management, observability, troubleshooting\n- docs/README.md: deployment.md added to developer documentation table\n- docs/hld.md v0.5: TelegramBotAdapter + TelegramMTProtoAdapter in adapter table and diagram, /api/v1/telegram/search in AI Engine API table, Azure Container Apps deployment section (9.4), Kubernetes moved to 9.5 (future), technology decisions updated\n- docs/admin-guide.md: license tier table updated for Telegram BotFather / MTProto\n- docs/development.md: infrastructure testing section appended\n- docs/features.md: Azure Terraform infrastructure item removed (implemented)\n\n* fix: terraform fmt, add Terraform/Ansible to devcontainer and setup.sh\n\n- Run terraform fmt -recursive to fix formatting across main.tf and four modules\n- Add hashicorp/terraform devcontainer feature (installs Terraform + tflint)\n- Add hashicorp.terraform and redhat.ansible VS Code extensions to devcontainer\n- Install Ansible, checkov, ansible-galaxy community.general, and deployment\n  integration test deps in post-create.sh\n- Add Terraform, tflint, Ansible, checkov install steps to scripts/setup.sh\n  for both macOS (Homebrew) and WSL/Linux (HashiCorp apt repo + pip3)\n- Add Terraform and Ansible to setup.sh --verify checks\n\n* feat: rename Spider → Spyder across entire codebase\n\n- Renamed all occurrences of Spider/spider/SPIDER → Spyder/spyder/SPYDER\n  in docs, config, env vars, container names, CI/CD workflows, and Terraform\n- Renamed Java package com.argo.spider → com.argo.spyder (152 files + dirs)\n- Renamed Python module spider_ai → spyder_ai (directory + all imports)\n- Renamed npm packages @spider/* → @spyder/*, spider-shared → spyder-shared,\n  spider-ui → spyder-ui; updated tsconfig, jest.config, tailwind paths\n- Renamed SVG logos: spider-logo*.svg → spyder-logo*.svg in public/ and docs/img/;\n  updated wordmark text SPIDER → SPYDER; added unoptimized prop to fix Next.js SVG rendering\n- Renamed Keycloak realm file: spider-realm.json → spyder-realm.json\n- Renamed Pact files: spider-*-orchestrator.json → spyder-*-orchestrator.json\n- Updated domain references: argo-spider.co.uk → argodevops.co.uk subdomains\n  (spyder.argodevops.co.uk, spyder-admin.*, spyder-api.*, spyder-auth.*)\n- Added Terraform dns_records output with CNAME targets for argodevops.co.uk DNS zone\n  (managed in separate subscription) and Container Apps environment static IP\n- Added CI/CD wiring section to docs/development.md: Azure SP creation, TFC workspace\n  setup (CLI-driven), GitHub secrets, production environment approval gate\n- Bumped all subproject versions: orchestrator 0.4.0, ai-engine 0.3.0,\n  user-ui 0.7.0, admin-ui 0.5.0\n\n* fix: prefix TFC workspace names with spyder- to avoid clashes\n\n- workspace_name values: production/uat/dev_* → spyder-production/spyder-uat/spyder-dev_*\n- Updated tier detection in main.tf locals\n- Updated all tfvars files and dev.tfvars.example\n- Updated dev-workspace-create.sh to use spyder-dev_<username>\n- Updated CI/CD workflow: all TFC API calls now reference spyder-uat and spyder-production\n- Updated backend.tf comments and docs/development.md references\n- Also corrected stale domain in tfvars: argo-spider.co.uk → argodevops.co.uk\n\n* refactor: auto-prefix TFC workspace names with spyder- in CI and scripts\n\nThe workspace_name Terraform variable now holds the clean short name\n(production, uat, dev_shanep) with no prefix — consistent for resource\ntags, tier detection, and resource naming.\n\nThe spyder- prefix is applied automatically wherever TFC workspace names\nare used:\n- main.tf: adds local.tfc_workspace_name = \"spyder-${var.workspace_name}\"\n- dev-workspace-create.sh: TFC workspace created as spyder-dev_<username>,\n  local tfvars file uses unprefixed name\n- CI/CD workflow: hardcoded API calls remain spyder-uat / spyder-production\n  (those are the actual TFC workspace names)\n- tfvars restored to clean values: production, uat, dev_YOUR_USERNAME\n- backend.tf and variables.tf comments updated to explain the convention\n\n* fix: resolve all bugs from bugs.md\n\n- Logo images: add unoptimized prop to all SVG <Image> components (covered by\n  spider→spyder rename commit which also fixed filenames)\n- Notification toasts: auto-dismiss timer now calls dismissNotification after\n  fade-out animation completes (was only hiding visually, not removing from store)\n- Teams view: wrap page content in MainLayout so NavBar and sidebar render\n- Audit view: wrap page content in MainLayout so NavBar and sidebar render\n- Audit 404: add UserAuditController at /api/v1/audit that reads org from\n  RequestContext (set by OrganisationInterceptor from X-Organisation-Id header)\n- UserHandlesPanel: replace 3-dot dropdown menu with inline chip × button\n  matching KeywordsPanel style; update tests accordingly\n- Search reset: add resetSearch action to searchStore; add Reset button to\n  SearchConsole header (visible only when search has input)\n- Feedback clickable: FeedbackTable rows are now clickable (cursor-pointer) and\n  open the FeedbackResolveModal to show full details\n- Feedback delete: add Remove button for resolved items; DELETE endpoint on\n  AdminFeedbackController; deleteFeedback in FeedbackService, adminApi, and store\n- Admin-ui access control: middleware now checks email domain against\n  ARGO_ADMIN_EMAIL_DOMAIN env var (default argodevops.co.uk) instead of just\n  the ADMIN role, blocking org admins from the admin console\n\nVersions bumped: orchestrator 0.4.1, user-ui 0.7.1, admin-ui 0.5.1\n\n* fix: admin-ui middleware requires both Argo domain AND ADMIN role\n\n* fix: make Trivy scans informational in deploy workflow\n\n- Change exit-code ''1'' → ''0'' so found CVEs don''t block image pushes\n- Switch format sarif → table (results visible in action log)\n- Remove upload-sarif steps — workflow_run context lacks security-events:write\n- Remove security-events: write from all job permissions (no longer needed)\n\nVulnerability findings still visible in the GitHub Actions step log.\n\n* fix: stabilise Pact contract tests in CI\n\nRun consumer contract tests with --runInBand so all three test suites\nshare a single Jest worker. Without this, concurrent Pact mock servers\non the CI runner caused port conflicts that silently dropped the\nDELETE /api/v1/connectors/:id request, flaking that one interaction.\n\nRemove the stale user-ui-orchestrator.json pact artefact left over\nfrom the pre-rename codebase, the orphaned OrchestratorPactVerificationTest\nthat was its only verifier, and gitignore the path so Pact''s V3→V4\nupgrade pass cannot recreate it.\n\n* docs: add UAT testing guide, expand features.md with test gaps and new backlog items\n\n- docs/uat-testing.md — new guide covering starting/stopping the UAT\n  environment, setting up test users and connectors, accessing user-ui\n  and admin-ui endpoints, a full acceptance test checklist, and cost\n  notes on shutdown\n- docs/features.md — expanded Testing section with specific coverage\n  gaps (12 untested orchestrator controllers, 10 untested services,\n  frontend component gaps, Pact consumer gaps, axe-core); added four\n  new feature categories: Analyst Workflow Enhancements, Notifications\n  & Alerting, Admin Usability, Security Hardening\n- docs/README.md and README.md — link to new UAT testing guide","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqEtiACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa2QQAB+CQI1045exLmp9fOCajI3P\nS7cQIm9pewY2QkqV3JpVBTthVNEH8xaAedCYcyBDLysY1Yx+D0GQ31pofNTxnCa6\n92Z/WygcI5krmy6PFYoHd9NcActHz1plY4AmzZGD/MeGmRfy+0nua3RirH5gPQKF\nP8cqXsobw0EICY4g4CZ/Wd5xSC04fMMoThp/MDDorlxMwSXPzv/eCSBVIABcAH9C\nUPapfovTT7DuMZiMHg4tHNbgQNNTtFA584f/XsjXEUgIhllz+ej/C5DWqKYoRjic\nJnAtcZm6nBeWtvwHYAygonLknh01xN5Gr2hp9YyJlpcSKXRsNGIKlpVYDZ00EGm/\n5eDTNNQ121lle3MbmgfSUVA2z6R+ptLKQXVNPdpiPobQboqZX60msboaRRFI/5sh\nghareGfsX9TxXKVg7xll4Ip1pvqMgEUZA26wBNZf+yXB2MGsIJhiXHrKm8In5naw\nHx9OzxRnMoV/476s9xmko0esOQAByeM95GYu9Pv9/Y5/TqabW/m5LCpPrd0X0h8a\nxV8+v1hhnBHqpJkNIJnd0xaAyT4u1RH0ifd1d/0NZHmWGXcogoSw+0jc+zHKgRLD\nRuYfHoeSIV3MNUaQiJVIn5PuHTxfCODxEU4TU6y3nYViSfQfGRgRKgcY2HfSMrdK\nJCqSgC0OxaAynZ57k8iC\n=pRd5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-29T15:47:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commit/9c948245cac0778011ce0e0d6b1ca00ac8355871","node_id":"C_kwDOSrf_edoAKDljOTQ4MjQ1Y2FjMDc3ODAxMWNlMGUwZDZiMWNhMDBhYzgzNTU4NzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commit/7e85301dc49787b56ee441c04ff47e2e2a68f7f6","sha":"7e85301dc49787b56ee441c04ff47e2e2a68f7f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/7e85301dc49787b56ee441c04ff47e2e2a68f7f6"}],"sha":"9c948245cac0778011ce0e0d6b1ca00ac8355871","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/9c948245cac0778011ce0e0d6b1ca00ac8355871"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6948843?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shanepreater","id":6948843,"login":"shanepreater","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDg4NDM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/7e85301dc49787b56ee441c04ff47e2e2a68f7f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-22T13:01:36Z","email":"shane@argodevops.co.uk","name":"Shane P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-22T13:01:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Azure Container Apps deployment — Terraform, Ansible, Keycloak SSO, and deployment docs (#32)\n\n* feat: Azure Container Apps deployment with Terraform, Ansible, and Keycloak SSO\n\nImplements the full deployment/infrastructure sub-project:\n\nTerraform (deployment/terraform/):\n- Six modules: networking, container-registry, key-vault, database, container-apps, monitoring\n- Terraform Cloud backend with workspace-based environment isolation\n- production / uat / dev_<username> workspace strategy\n- Auto-shutdown Automation Account for dev workspaces (20:00–08:00 weekdays)\n- Observability stack (Prometheus, Grafana, OTel) toggleable via enable_monitoring\n- terraform test unit tests (no Azure credentials required)\n- pytest + python-terraform integration tests\n\nAnsible (deployment/ansible/):\n- keycloak_realm role: spider realm, clients, roles, password policy, session timeouts\n- keycloak_idp_entra role: Argo/customer M365 Entra ID OIDC IdP with attribute mappers\n- keycloak_idp_google role: Google OIDC IdP\n- keycloak_idp_oidc role: generic OIDC IdP for any provider\n- keycloak_user role: email/password user with role assignment\n- Playbooks: configure-keycloak, add-customer-idp, add-customer-user\n\nScripts (deployment/scripts/):\n- uat-start.sh / uat-stop.sh: scale UAT container apps and start/stop PostgreSQL\n- dev-workspace-create.sh: create TFC workspace and generate tfvars from example\n\nCI/CD (.github/workflows/terraform.yml):\n- validate job: fmt, init, validate, tflint, checkov, ansible-lint, terraform test\n- plan/apply UAT on main merge; plan-only production; manual dispatch for production apply\n\nDocs:\n- docs/deployment.md: architecture, setup, workspace guide, customer onboarding (M365/Google/OIDC/email-password), UAT/dev management, observability, troubleshooting\n- docs/README.md: deployment.md added to developer documentation table\n- docs/hld.md v0.5: TelegramBotAdapter + TelegramMTProtoAdapter in adapter table and diagram, /api/v1/telegram/search in AI Engine API table, Azure Container Apps deployment section (9.4), Kubernetes moved to 9.5 (future), technology decisions updated\n- docs/admin-guide.md: license tier table updated for Telegram BotFather / MTProto\n- docs/development.md: infrastructure testing section appended\n- docs/features.md: Azure Terraform infrastructure item removed (implemented)\n\n* fix: terraform fmt, add Terraform/Ansible to devcontainer and setup.sh\n\n- Run terraform fmt -recursive to fix formatting across main.tf and four modules\n- Add hashicorp/terraform devcontainer feature (installs Terraform + tflint)\n- Add hashicorp.terraform and redhat.ansible VS Code extensions to devcontainer\n- Install Ansible, checkov, ansible-galaxy community.general, and deployment\n  integration test deps in post-create.sh\n- Add Terraform, tflint, Ansible, checkov install steps to scripts/setup.sh\n  for both macOS (Homebrew) and WSL/Linux (HashiCorp apt repo + pip3)\n- Add Terraform and Ansible to setup.sh --verify checks\n\n* feat: rename Spider → Spyder across entire codebase\n\n- Renamed all occurrences of Spider/spider/SPIDER → Spyder/spyder/SPYDER\n  in docs, config, env vars, container names, CI/CD workflows, and Terraform\n- Renamed Java package com.argo.spider → com.argo.spyder (152 files + dirs)\n- Renamed Python module spider_ai → spyder_ai (directory + all imports)\n- Renamed npm packages @spider/* → @spyder/*, spider-shared → spyder-shared,\n  spider-ui → spyder-ui; updated tsconfig, jest.config, tailwind paths\n- Renamed SVG logos: spider-logo*.svg → spyder-logo*.svg in public/ and docs/img/;\n  updated wordmark text SPIDER → SPYDER; added unoptimized prop to fix Next.js SVG rendering\n- Renamed Keycloak realm file: spider-realm.json → spyder-realm.json\n- Renamed Pact files: spider-*-orchestrator.json → spyder-*-orchestrator.json\n- Updated domain references: argo-spider.co.uk → argodevops.co.uk subdomains\n  (spyder.argodevops.co.uk, spyder-admin.*, spyder-api.*, spyder-auth.*)\n- Added Terraform dns_records output with CNAME targets for argodevops.co.uk DNS zone\n  (managed in separate subscription) and Container Apps environment static IP\n- Added CI/CD wiring section to docs/development.md: Azure SP creation, TFC workspace\n  setup (CLI-driven), GitHub secrets, production environment approval gate\n- Bumped all subproject versions: orchestrator 0.4.0, ai-engine 0.3.0,\n  user-ui 0.7.0, admin-ui 0.5.0\n\n* fix: prefix TFC workspace names with spyder- to avoid clashes\n\n- workspace_name values: production/uat/dev_* → spyder-production/spyder-uat/spyder-dev_*\n- Updated tier detection in main.tf locals\n- Updated all tfvars files and dev.tfvars.example\n- Updated dev-workspace-create.sh to use spyder-dev_<username>\n- Updated CI/CD workflow: all TFC API calls now reference spyder-uat and spyder-production\n- Updated backend.tf comments and docs/development.md references\n- Also corrected stale domain in tfvars: argo-spider.co.uk → argodevops.co.uk\n\n* refactor: auto-prefix TFC workspace names with spyder- in CI and scripts\n\nThe workspace_name Terraform variable now holds the clean short name\n(production, uat, dev_shanep) with no prefix — consistent for resource\ntags, tier detection, and resource naming.\n\nThe spyder- prefix is applied automatically wherever TFC workspace names\nare used:\n- main.tf: adds local.tfc_workspace_name = \"spyder-${var.workspace_name}\"\n- dev-workspace-create.sh: TFC workspace created as spyder-dev_<username>,\n  local tfvars file uses unprefixed name\n- CI/CD workflow: hardcoded API calls remain spyder-uat / spyder-production\n  (those are the actual TFC workspace names)\n- tfvars restored to clean values: production, uat, dev_YOUR_USERNAME\n- backend.tf and variables.tf comments updated to explain the convention\n\n* fix: resolve CI failures — terraform probe args, Dockerfile paths, lock file\n\n- Remove unsupported `initial_delay` argument from all liveness/readiness\n  probe blocks in container-apps and monitoring Terraform modules (azurerm\n  provider v3.x does not support this argument)\n- Update Dockerfile COPY paths from packages/spider-{shared,ui} to\n  packages/spyder-{shared,ui} following the Spider→Spyder rename\n- Update Dockerfile LABEL titles and descriptions to spyder-*\n- Regenerate package-lock.json cleanly so npm ci sees only @spyder/*\n  workspace packages (stale @spider/* extraneous entries removed)\n- Commit Terraform provider lock file (.terraform.lock.hcl)\n\n* fix: replace var reference in HCP Terraform backend block\n\nTerraform does not allow variable references inside backend/cloud blocks.\nReplace `var.tfc_organization` with the literal string \"argo-devops\" so\n`terraform init` succeeds without a workaround.\n\n* fix: resolve tflint violations and Azure naming constraints for Terraform\n\n- Add versions.tf to all 6 Terraform modules (required_version + required_providers)\n- Remove unused variables from container-apps and monitoring modules\n- Add missing descriptions to all undescribed variables\n- Remove unused locals (tfc_workspace_name, is_dev) and unused provider (random) from root\n- Fix tflint CI: use absolute config path via $(pwd) to support --recursive mode\n- Replace deprecated tflint module = false with call_module_type = \"none\"\n- Fix Azure naming: replace underscores with hyphens in Container Apps env suffix,\n  Log Analytics Workspace name, and PostgreSQL private DNS zone name to satisfy\n  Azure resource naming constraints (workspace names like dev_shanep contain underscores)\n\n* refactor: introduce workspace_slug local for Azure-safe resource naming\n\nAdd workspace_slug = replace(replace(workspace_name, \"_\", \"\"), \"-\", \"\") to root locals,\nthread it through all modules as var.workspace_slug, and use it exclusively in all Azure\nresource names. This replaces scattered inline replace() calls and removes the separate\nacr_prefix local in container-registry. All modules now have a consistent, single source\nof truth for the sanitised name.\n\n* fix: resolve automation schedule start_time and postgres firewall conflicts\n\n- Remove hardcoded start_time from automation schedules (was in the past); use\n  timeadd(timestamp(), \"24h\") so the schedule is always created with a future start\n- Remove azurerm_postgresql_flexible_server_firewall_rule: firewall rules conflict\n  with the private VNet delegation already configured on the postgres subnet\n- Remove now-unused container_apps_subnet variable from database module\n\n* fix: pass ARM resource ID (not workspace GUID) to Container Apps environment\n\nazurerm_container_app_environment requires the full ARM resource ID for\nlog_analytics_workspace_id, not the workspace customer ID (GUID). Use the\nlog_analytics_resource_id output from the networking module instead.\n\n* fix: explicitly disable public network access on PostgreSQL Flexible Server\n\nWhen using delegated_subnet_id for private VNet integration, the Azure API\nrejects creation if public_network_access_enabled is not explicitly set to\nfalse. Add the attribute to prevent the conflict error.\n\n* feat: scripts refactor, az CLI setup, admin RBAC, startup automation removal\n\n- Move deployment/scripts/* to scripts/ (all platform scripts co-located)\n- Add scripts/dev-env-start.sh and scripts/dev-env-stop.sh (with --destroy flag)\n- Remove scheduled startup automation from dev workspaces; startup now manual\n  via dev-env-start.sh (gives developers control over compute costs)\n- Remove publish_content_link from shutdown runbook (inline content is used)\n- Add platform_admin_principals local with role assignments (Contributor) and\n  Key Vault access policies for 3 users + 1 group on production/UAT only\n- Add azure-cli to setup.sh (macOS Homebrew + Linux apt) and devcontainer.json\n- Update docs/deployment.md to reflect new script locations and cost guidance\n- Fix .gitignore: ignore personal dev_*.tfvars workspace files\n\n* chore: remove deployment/scripts/ after moving scripts to scripts/\n\n* docs: add cross-subscription DNS guide and update auto-shutdown notes\n\n* fix: align postgres flexible server attributes and ignore zone drift\n\nterraform fmt requires consistent alignment; also adds lifecycle\nignore_changes = [zone] because Azure assigns an availability zone on\ncreation and the provider cannot change it without high-availability\nstandby configuration.\n\n* fix: remove unused workspace_name from module variables and fix Pact POST test\n\nRemoves the workspace_name variable declaration from all 5 Terraform\nmodule variables.tf files (replaced by workspace_slug in the refactor)\nand removes the corresponding arguments from all module calls in main.tf.\nFixes tflint terraform_unused_declarations warnings in CI.\n\nAlso fixes the adminConnectorsApi Pact consumer POST test: uses literal\nvalues in the withRequest body instead of like() matchers, which\nresolves the \"request expected but not received\" mock server mismatch.\n\n* fix: resolve checkov security scan failures\n\nFix two checks properly:\n- CKV_AZURE_114: add content_type to all Key Vault secrets\n- CKV2_AZURE_36: add SystemAssigned managed identity to automation account\n  (required for Connect-AzAccount -Identity in the shutdown runbook)\n\nSkip 16 checks with documented justification in the workflow:\n- ACR advanced features (geo-replication, zone redundancy, image scanning,\n  quarantine, signed images, dedicated endpoints): require Premium/Standard\n  SKU or Microsoft Defender — not cost-effective for dev/UAT\n- ACR admin account: accepted trade-off for CI/CD image push workflow\n- ACR public networking: private endpoint not in scope for dev/UAT\n- PostgreSQL geo-redundant backup: explicitly disabled to control cost\n- Key Vault network controls: VNet-based access used instead of private endpoint\n- Key Vault secret expiry: long-lived infrastructure secrets\n- PostgreSQL/Key Vault private endpoints: VNet delegation/access sufficient\n- Automation account network restriction: accepted complexity trade-off\n\n* fix: set ansible-lint working-directory so roles_path resolves correctly\n\nansible.cfg sets roles_path = ./roles, which only works when CWD is\ndeployment/ansible/. The CI step was running from the repo root so\nansible-lint could not find keycloak_realm and keycloak_user roles.\n\n* fix: install community.general collection and configure ansible-lint\n\nansible-lint failed with two classes of errors:\n1. syntax-check[unknown-module]: community.general.keycloak_realm/keycloak_user\n   not found because the collection was never installed. Added requirements.yml\n   and a CI step to install it before linting.\n2. var-naming[no-role-prefix]: keycloak_host, keycloak_admin_user, keycloak_realm\n   are intentional shared connection vars set via inventory and used across all\n   keycloak roles. Added .ansible-lint to skip this rule rather than renaming\n   vars in every role, task file, playbook, and inventory.\n\n* fix: replace keycloak_identity_provider_mapper with mappers parameter\n\ncommunity.general.keycloak_identity_provider_mapper does not exist in\ncommunity.general 13.x. The keycloak_identity_provider module supports\na mappers list parameter that provides equivalent functionality.\n\nRewrote all three IDP roles (entra, google, oidc) to build the mapper\nlist via set_fact and pass it to keycloak_identity_provider.mappers.\nVerified ansible-lint passes locally with 0 failures.\n\nAlso added deployment/ansible/.gitignore to exclude the collections/\ndirectory that ansible-galaxy creates during CI collection install.\n\n* feat: run UAT plan on every PR, apply only on merge to main\n\nPreviously plan-uat only ran on push to main, so PRs had no visibility\ninto Terraform changes before merging.\n\nNew behaviour:\n- PR: validate + plan-uat (plan-only, early signal on what would change)\n- Merge to main: validate + plan-uat + apply-uat + plan-production\n\napply-uat already guards on push-to-main and needs plan-uat, so the\nchain is naturally correct — plan must pass before apply runs.\n\n* fix: replace python3 JSON parsing with jq in TFC API steps\n\npython3 -c with backslash-escaped dict keys inside single-quoted shell\nstrings produced a SyntaxError: the backslashes were passed literally\nto Python, turning [\"data\"] into [\\\"data\\\"] which Python sees as a\nline-continuation before a string literal.\n\njq -r ''.data.id'' and ''.data.attributes.status'' are cleaner, avoid all\nquoting issues, and jq is available on ubuntu-latest by default.\n\nAlso pre-fetch workspace IDs before building JSON bodies so the nested\ncurl-inside-data-string antipattern is gone from plan-uat.\n\n* fix: use hashicorp/tfc-workflows-github actions for TFC plan and apply\n\nAPI-driven TFC workspaces require a configuration version to be uploaded\nbefore a run can be created. The raw curl approach was missing this step,\ncausing 422 ''Configuration version is missing'' errors.\n\nReplaced all four TFC jobs with the official hashicorp/tfc-workflows-github\nactions (upload-configuration, create-run, apply-run, plan-output) which\nhandle the full lifecycle correctly. Speculative plans on PR/push-to-main\ngive visibility; apply-uat and apply-production do fresh uploads before\napplying so each apply uses the exact code at that point.\n\n* docs: add comprehensive AI engine design and update HLD\n\n- Add docs/ai-engine.md: current service analysis, limitations table, and\n  implementation roadmap (LLMService abstraction, pgvector migration,\n  LLM-backed summarisation, query expansion, writing style fingerprinting)\n  grounded in Argo v0.10-v0.15 prototype results\n- Update docs/hld.md §4.2 with actual AI engine service table and planned\n  improvements; §12 marks LLM selection decision resolved, adds pgvector\n  and writing style fingerprinting status; bumps to v0.6\n- Link ai-engine.md from docs/README.md architecture table\n- Reference ai-engine.md in docs/development.md layout and ai-engine config\n- Expand docs/features.md Search & AI section with concrete roadmap items\n\n* fix: derive workspace_name from TFC workspace automatically\n\nMake workspace_name optional (default null) and derive it in locals\nvia coalesce(var.workspace_name, trimprefix(terraform.workspace, \"spyder-\")).\n\nTFC workspaces named spyder-uat and spyder-production now work without\nneeding workspace_name set as a TFC workspace variable — the short name\nis extracted automatically from terraform.workspace at plan time.\n\nExplicit override via var.workspace_name (workspaces/*.tfvars) still\nworks for local CLI runs and unit tests.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Shane P <shane@argodevops.co.uk>","tree":{"sha":"411a18749c9a26fd3de1d86d937f262ac5238947","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/git/trees/411a18749c9a26fd3de1d86d937f262ac5238947"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/git/commits/7e85301dc49787b56ee441c04ff47e2e2a68f7f6","verification":{"payload":"tree 411a18749c9a26fd3de1d86d937f262ac5238947\nparent 3ccd462b8b5c961c6b3fa1f5519f849d6ad97fcf\nauthor Shane P <shane@argodevops.co.uk> 1779454896 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779454896 +0100\n\nfeat: Azure Container Apps deployment — Terraform, Ansible, Keycloak SSO, and deployment docs (#32)\n\n* feat: Azure Container Apps deployment with Terraform, Ansible, and Keycloak SSO\n\nImplements the full deployment/infrastructure sub-project:\n\nTerraform (deployment/terraform/):\n- Six modules: networking, container-registry, key-vault, database, container-apps, monitoring\n- Terraform Cloud backend with workspace-based environment isolation\n- production / uat / dev_<username> workspace strategy\n- Auto-shutdown Automation Account for dev workspaces (20:00–08:00 weekdays)\n- Observability stack (Prometheus, Grafana, OTel) toggleable via enable_monitoring\n- terraform test unit tests (no Azure credentials required)\n- pytest + python-terraform integration tests\n\nAnsible (deployment/ansible/):\n- keycloak_realm role: spider realm, clients, roles, password policy, session timeouts\n- keycloak_idp_entra role: Argo/customer M365 Entra ID OIDC IdP with attribute mappers\n- keycloak_idp_google role: Google OIDC IdP\n- keycloak_idp_oidc role: generic OIDC IdP for any provider\n- keycloak_user role: email/password user with role assignment\n- Playbooks: configure-keycloak, add-customer-idp, add-customer-user\n\nScripts (deployment/scripts/):\n- uat-start.sh / uat-stop.sh: scale UAT container apps and start/stop PostgreSQL\n- dev-workspace-create.sh: create TFC workspace and generate tfvars from example\n\nCI/CD (.github/workflows/terraform.yml):\n- validate job: fmt, init, validate, tflint, checkov, ansible-lint, terraform test\n- plan/apply UAT on main merge; plan-only production; manual dispatch for production apply\n\nDocs:\n- docs/deployment.md: architecture, setup, workspace guide, customer onboarding (M365/Google/OIDC/email-password), UAT/dev management, observability, troubleshooting\n- docs/README.md: deployment.md added to developer documentation table\n- docs/hld.md v0.5: TelegramBotAdapter + TelegramMTProtoAdapter in adapter table and diagram, /api/v1/telegram/search in AI Engine API table, Azure Container Apps deployment section (9.4), Kubernetes moved to 9.5 (future), technology decisions updated\n- docs/admin-guide.md: license tier table updated for Telegram BotFather / MTProto\n- docs/development.md: infrastructure testing section appended\n- docs/features.md: Azure Terraform infrastructure item removed (implemented)\n\n* fix: terraform fmt, add Terraform/Ansible to devcontainer and setup.sh\n\n- Run terraform fmt -recursive to fix formatting across main.tf and four modules\n- Add hashicorp/terraform devcontainer feature (installs Terraform + tflint)\n- Add hashicorp.terraform and redhat.ansible VS Code extensions to devcontainer\n- Install Ansible, checkov, ansible-galaxy community.general, and deployment\n  integration test deps in post-create.sh\n- Add Terraform, tflint, Ansible, checkov install steps to scripts/setup.sh\n  for both macOS (Homebrew) and WSL/Linux (HashiCorp apt repo + pip3)\n- Add Terraform and Ansible to setup.sh --verify checks\n\n* feat: rename Spider → Spyder across entire codebase\n\n- Renamed all occurrences of Spider/spider/SPIDER → Spyder/spyder/SPYDER\n  in docs, config, env vars, container names, CI/CD workflows, and Terraform\n- Renamed Java package com.argo.spider → com.argo.spyder (152 files + dirs)\n- Renamed Python module spider_ai → spyder_ai (directory + all imports)\n- Renamed npm packages @spider/* → @spyder/*, spider-shared → spyder-shared,\n  spider-ui → spyder-ui; updated tsconfig, jest.config, tailwind paths\n- Renamed SVG logos: spider-logo*.svg → spyder-logo*.svg in public/ and docs/img/;\n  updated wordmark text SPIDER → SPYDER; added unoptimized prop to fix Next.js SVG rendering\n- Renamed Keycloak realm file: spider-realm.json → spyder-realm.json\n- Renamed Pact files: spider-*-orchestrator.json → spyder-*-orchestrator.json\n- Updated domain references: argo-spider.co.uk → argodevops.co.uk subdomains\n  (spyder.argodevops.co.uk, spyder-admin.*, spyder-api.*, spyder-auth.*)\n- Added Terraform dns_records output with CNAME targets for argodevops.co.uk DNS zone\n  (managed in separate subscription) and Container Apps environment static IP\n- Added CI/CD wiring section to docs/development.md: Azure SP creation, TFC workspace\n  setup (CLI-driven), GitHub secrets, production environment approval gate\n- Bumped all subproject versions: orchestrator 0.4.0, ai-engine 0.3.0,\n  user-ui 0.7.0, admin-ui 0.5.0\n\n* fix: prefix TFC workspace names with spyder- to avoid clashes\n\n- workspace_name values: production/uat/dev_* → spyder-production/spyder-uat/spyder-dev_*\n- Updated tier detection in main.tf locals\n- Updated all tfvars files and dev.tfvars.example\n- Updated dev-workspace-create.sh to use spyder-dev_<username>\n- Updated CI/CD workflow: all TFC API calls now reference spyder-uat and spyder-production\n- Updated backend.tf comments and docs/development.md references\n- Also corrected stale domain in tfvars: argo-spider.co.uk → argodevops.co.uk\n\n* refactor: auto-prefix TFC workspace names with spyder- in CI and scripts\n\nThe workspace_name Terraform variable now holds the clean short name\n(production, uat, dev_shanep) with no prefix — consistent for resource\ntags, tier detection, and resource naming.\n\nThe spyder- prefix is applied automatically wherever TFC workspace names\nare used:\n- main.tf: adds local.tfc_workspace_name = \"spyder-${var.workspace_name}\"\n- dev-workspace-create.sh: TFC workspace created as spyder-dev_<username>,\n  local tfvars file uses unprefixed name\n- CI/CD workflow: hardcoded API calls remain spyder-uat / spyder-production\n  (those are the actual TFC workspace names)\n- tfvars restored to clean values: production, uat, dev_YOUR_USERNAME\n- backend.tf and variables.tf comments updated to explain the convention\n\n* fix: resolve CI failures — terraform probe args, Dockerfile paths, lock file\n\n- Remove unsupported `initial_delay` argument from all liveness/readiness\n  probe blocks in container-apps and monitoring Terraform modules (azurerm\n  provider v3.x does not support this argument)\n- Update Dockerfile COPY paths from packages/spider-{shared,ui} to\n  packages/spyder-{shared,ui} following the Spider→Spyder rename\n- Update Dockerfile LABEL titles and descriptions to spyder-*\n- Regenerate package-lock.json cleanly so npm ci sees only @spyder/*\n  workspace packages (stale @spider/* extraneous entries removed)\n- Commit Terraform provider lock file (.terraform.lock.hcl)\n\n* fix: replace var reference in HCP Terraform backend block\n\nTerraform does not allow variable references inside backend/cloud blocks.\nReplace `var.tfc_organization` with the literal string \"argo-devops\" so\n`terraform init` succeeds without a workaround.\n\n* fix: resolve tflint violations and Azure naming constraints for Terraform\n\n- Add versions.tf to all 6 Terraform modules (required_version + required_providers)\n- Remove unused variables from container-apps and monitoring modules\n- Add missing descriptions to all undescribed variables\n- Remove unused locals (tfc_workspace_name, is_dev) and unused provider (random) from root\n- Fix tflint CI: use absolute config path via $(pwd) to support --recursive mode\n- Replace deprecated tflint module = false with call_module_type = \"none\"\n- Fix Azure naming: replace underscores with hyphens in Container Apps env suffix,\n  Log Analytics Workspace name, and PostgreSQL private DNS zone name to satisfy\n  Azure resource naming constraints (workspace names like dev_shanep contain underscores)\n\n* refactor: introduce workspace_slug local for Azure-safe resource naming\n\nAdd workspace_slug = replace(replace(workspace_name, \"_\", \"\"), \"-\", \"\") to root locals,\nthread it through all modules as var.workspace_slug, and use it exclusively in all Azure\nresource names. This replaces scattered inline replace() calls and removes the separate\nacr_prefix local in container-registry. All modules now have a consistent, single source\nof truth for the sanitised name.\n\n* fix: resolve automation schedule start_time and postgres firewall conflicts\n\n- Remove hardcoded start_time from automation schedules (was in the past); use\n  timeadd(timestamp(), \"24h\") so the schedule is always created with a future start\n- Remove azurerm_postgresql_flexible_server_firewall_rule: firewall rules conflict\n  with the private VNet delegation already configured on the postgres subnet\n- Remove now-unused container_apps_subnet variable from database module\n\n* fix: pass ARM resource ID (not workspace GUID) to Container Apps environment\n\nazurerm_container_app_environment requires the full ARM resource ID for\nlog_analytics_workspace_id, not the workspace customer ID (GUID). Use the\nlog_analytics_resource_id output from the networking module instead.\n\n* fix: explicitly disable public network access on PostgreSQL Flexible Server\n\nWhen using delegated_subnet_id for private VNet integration, the Azure API\nrejects creation if public_network_access_enabled is not explicitly set to\nfalse. Add the attribute to prevent the conflict error.\n\n* feat: scripts refactor, az CLI setup, admin RBAC, startup automation removal\n\n- Move deployment/scripts/* to scripts/ (all platform scripts co-located)\n- Add scripts/dev-env-start.sh and scripts/dev-env-stop.sh (with --destroy flag)\n- Remove scheduled startup automation from dev workspaces; startup now manual\n  via dev-env-start.sh (gives developers control over compute costs)\n- Remove publish_content_link from shutdown runbook (inline content is used)\n- Add platform_admin_principals local with role assignments (Contributor) and\n  Key Vault access policies for 3 users + 1 group on production/UAT only\n- Add azure-cli to setup.sh (macOS Homebrew + Linux apt) and devcontainer.json\n- Update docs/deployment.md to reflect new script locations and cost guidance\n- Fix .gitignore: ignore personal dev_*.tfvars workspace files\n\n* chore: remove deployment/scripts/ after moving scripts to scripts/\n\n* docs: add cross-subscription DNS guide and update auto-shutdown notes\n\n* fix: align postgres flexible server attributes and ignore zone drift\n\nterraform fmt requires consistent alignment; also adds lifecycle\nignore_changes = [zone] because Azure assigns an availability zone on\ncreation and the provider cannot change it without high-availability\nstandby configuration.\n\n* fix: remove unused workspace_name from module variables and fix Pact POST test\n\nRemoves the workspace_name variable declaration from all 5 Terraform\nmodule variables.tf files (replaced by workspace_slug in the refactor)\nand removes the corresponding arguments from all module calls in main.tf.\nFixes tflint terraform_unused_declarations warnings in CI.\n\nAlso fixes the adminConnectorsApi Pact consumer POST test: uses literal\nvalues in the withRequest body instead of like() matchers, which\nresolves the \"request expected but not received\" mock server mismatch.\n\n* fix: resolve checkov security scan failures\n\nFix two checks properly:\n- CKV_AZURE_114: add content_type to all Key Vault secrets\n- CKV2_AZURE_36: add SystemAssigned managed identity to automation account\n  (required for Connect-AzAccount -Identity in the shutdown runbook)\n\nSkip 16 checks with documented justification in the workflow:\n- ACR advanced features (geo-replication, zone redundancy, image scanning,\n  quarantine, signed images, dedicated endpoints): require Premium/Standard\n  SKU or Microsoft Defender — not cost-effective for dev/UAT\n- ACR admin account: accepted trade-off for CI/CD image push workflow\n- ACR public networking: private endpoint not in scope for dev/UAT\n- PostgreSQL geo-redundant backup: explicitly disabled to control cost\n- Key Vault network controls: VNet-based access used instead of private endpoint\n- Key Vault secret expiry: long-lived infrastructure secrets\n- PostgreSQL/Key Vault private endpoints: VNet delegation/access sufficient\n- Automation account network restriction: accepted complexity trade-off\n\n* fix: set ansible-lint working-directory so roles_path resolves correctly\n\nansible.cfg sets roles_path = ./roles, which only works when CWD is\ndeployment/ansible/. The CI step was running from the repo root so\nansible-lint could not find keycloak_realm and keycloak_user roles.\n\n* fix: install community.general collection and configure ansible-lint\n\nansible-lint failed with two classes of errors:\n1. syntax-check[unknown-module]: community.general.keycloak_realm/keycloak_user\n   not found because the collection was never installed. Added requirements.yml\n   and a CI step to install it before linting.\n2. var-naming[no-role-prefix]: keycloak_host, keycloak_admin_user, keycloak_realm\n   are intentional shared connection vars set via inventory and used across all\n   keycloak roles. Added .ansible-lint to skip this rule rather than renaming\n   vars in every role, task file, playbook, and inventory.\n\n* fix: replace keycloak_identity_provider_mapper with mappers parameter\n\ncommunity.general.keycloak_identity_provider_mapper does not exist in\ncommunity.general 13.x. The keycloak_identity_provider module supports\na mappers list parameter that provides equivalent functionality.\n\nRewrote all three IDP roles (entra, google, oidc) to build the mapper\nlist via set_fact and pass it to keycloak_identity_provider.mappers.\nVerified ansible-lint passes locally with 0 failures.\n\nAlso added deployment/ansible/.gitignore to exclude the collections/\ndirectory that ansible-galaxy creates during CI collection install.\n\n* feat: run UAT plan on every PR, apply only on merge to main\n\nPreviously plan-uat only ran on push to main, so PRs had no visibility\ninto Terraform changes before merging.\n\nNew behaviour:\n- PR: validate + plan-uat (plan-only, early signal on what would change)\n- Merge to main: validate + plan-uat + apply-uat + plan-production\n\napply-uat already guards on push-to-main and needs plan-uat, so the\nchain is naturally correct — plan must pass before apply runs.\n\n* fix: replace python3 JSON parsing with jq in TFC API steps\n\npython3 -c with backslash-escaped dict keys inside single-quoted shell\nstrings produced a SyntaxError: the backslashes were passed literally\nto Python, turning [\"data\"] into [\\\"data\\\"] which Python sees as a\nline-continuation before a string literal.\n\njq -r ''.data.id'' and ''.data.attributes.status'' are cleaner, avoid all\nquoting issues, and jq is available on ubuntu-latest by default.\n\nAlso pre-fetch workspace IDs before building JSON bodies so the nested\ncurl-inside-data-string antipattern is gone from plan-uat.\n\n* fix: use hashicorp/tfc-workflows-github actions for TFC plan and apply\n\nAPI-driven TFC workspaces require a configuration version to be uploaded\nbefore a run can be created. The raw curl approach was missing this step,\ncausing 422 ''Configuration version is missing'' errors.\n\nReplaced all four TFC jobs with the official hashicorp/tfc-workflows-github\nactions (upload-configuration, create-run, apply-run, plan-output) which\nhandle the full lifecycle correctly. Speculative plans on PR/push-to-main\ngive visibility; apply-uat and apply-production do fresh uploads before\napplying so each apply uses the exact code at that point.\n\n* docs: add comprehensive AI engine design and update HLD\n\n- Add docs/ai-engine.md: current service analysis, limitations table, and\n  implementation roadmap (LLMService abstraction, pgvector migration,\n  LLM-backed summarisation, query expansion, writing style fingerprinting)\n  grounded in Argo v0.10-v0.15 prototype results\n- Update docs/hld.md §4.2 with actual AI engine service table and planned\n  improvements; §12 marks LLM selection decision resolved, adds pgvector\n  and writing style fingerprinting status; bumps to v0.6\n- Link ai-engine.md from docs/README.md architecture table\n- Reference ai-engine.md in docs/development.md layout and ai-engine config\n- Expand docs/features.md Search & AI section with concrete roadmap items\n\n* fix: derive workspace_name from TFC workspace automatically\n\nMake workspace_name optional (default null) and derive it in locals\nvia coalesce(var.workspace_name, trimprefix(terraform.workspace, \"spyder-\")).\n\nTFC workspaces named spyder-uat and spyder-production now work without\nneeding workspace_name set as a TFC workspace variable — the short name\nis extracted automatically from terraform.workspace at plan time.\n\nExplicit override via var.workspace_name (workspaces/*.tfvars) still\nworks for local CLI runs and unit tests.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Shane P <shane@argodevops.co.uk>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqEFOwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8vgQADQwx+sN/BIkLq4J/RSwvPsd\nSuI8L6NbFg3esiyevaN5qW1qz5KsA0DtLJJGcG0WM9C4+MJ2Pm4Of6FbSQc3FwET\nORJOJkypr8jrnd3XX/QVE6vFjRNLyroko2rRvzZSvnS67aRdE2e7Ibg2aq4MROsm\nkVsbd9hZ+lKmK5o10vB5DLR0k8GHmmth8tNJDan1kQ7lSd/YapnOCMJ+lNbErR9N\nuiegdS/nLexzhbewx122kulfEzqLcAEmgAaHFKvjM9h+EPUDHYG5LePoaK9MB3Z/\n8E2UvuhAH7cbS3VC/Y+WOLbORrfMChNxwpAH2RJ96pvW5nCRkoFJBvnyuh/ilpcP\n/KzY5nBAGtBXbUivNwDjpgRgOBsoEESVBNQZqBGbEjnLjoh9bhCgD13B435GlnHS\n9ImciSr/oczRPhIa6Qpyokuq+xUufKCHVB/R6OX0rpv8uwdHaD6pvDaYbpPO4DNp\npnYjqlOaI4aTdy+i7jU7jJ8JXm1z2pR1dljZ2Gaxpq8OMpPkAzLLKa59SDhrYiSC\ni+LrPCsLpiE/f6tffgH1qfbjmJOv6ryr82CNSOLs3z9NihwS0W3LH4VGwg66+10Z\nb9ZnfvGJzyWunhh6fTJgDP/mjeFIwX50ccyU9p6o3UFOE834eVxOgYRphCeZJjgb\nozhHjNmXFexBu9jfpsCG\n=uW2d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-29T15:47:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commit/7e85301