2a0d8d9321245cf45dbc73ad6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/42264bc9e9f983c2a0d8d9321245cf45dbc73ad6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6948843?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shanepreater","id":6948843,"login":"shanepreater","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDg4NDM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/b51d51bba3dc08e122bbd52d6cb2052b92148ebd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-20T17:24:53Z","email":"shane@argodevops.co.uk","name":"Shane P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-20T17:24:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve user-ui and admin-ui local-dev and Docker setup issues (#30)\n\n* fix: resolve user-ui and admin-ui local-dev and Docker issues\n\nDockerfile static assets (both UIs):\n  outputFileTracingRoot points to the monorepo root, so the standalone\n  build mirrors the full tree and server.js lands at ./user-ui/server.js.\n  Static files must be at ./user-ui/.next/static (not ./.next/static) or\n  the browser gets 404s for all CSS/JS assets.\n\n.env.example — Keycloak URLs now uncommented with local-dev defaults:\n  KEYCLOAK_EXTERNAL_URL / KEYCLOAK_INTERNAL_URL were missing entirely,\n  causing buildAuthOptions() to crash with \"Invalid URL: undefined/...\"\n  on first request. Also unblock NEXTAUTH_USER_UI_URL, NEXTAUTH_ADMIN_UI_URL,\n  KEYCLOAK_USER_UI_SECRET, KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_UI_SECRET with their dev defaults.\n\nstart-debug.sh — per-service Keycloak client IDs:\n  user-ui and admin-ui use different Keycloak clients (spider-user-ui /\n  spider-admin-ui). Inline the client-specific env vars before each npm\n  run dev invocation so both UIs get the right credentials without\n  conflicting through the shared .env.\n\nadmin-ui forbidden page:\n  Replace the static \"contact your administrator\" text with a\n  \"Copy my email address\" button so non-admin users can easily share\n  their account email when requesting access.\n\n* docs: add gotcha for start-debug.sh blank screen / Invalid URL after first setup\n\n* fix: web search returns no results; Pact tests fail with H2 seeds\n\nWebSearchAdapter: DuckDuckGo HTML endpoint silently redirects to its\nhomepage when sent a non-browser User-Agent or missing Accept headers.\nJsoup was sending only the Spider bot UA; added Accept and Accept-Language\nheaders matching a standard browser request so actual results are returned.\n\nPact provider tests: application.yml now defaults flyway.locations to\ninclude db/seed/h2, causing both @SpringBootTest-based provider tests to\nrun the V1000 seed which renames the Acme org and breaks the\nadminLicenseExists interaction. Added spring.flyway.locations=classpath:db/migration\nto both provider test @SpringBootTest properties.\n\ntest.sh: added _pact_report() to show per-interaction pass/fail after\nprovider verification, even when the step fails.\n\n* fix: Telegram returns no results for channel posts; audit fails in async thread\n\nTelegramAdapter: Telegram sends channel posts as \"channel_post\" in the\nupdate object, not \"message\". The adapter only checked update.get(\"message\")\nso every channel post was silently skipped. Fixed to fall back to\n\"channel_post\" when \"message\" is absent. Also fixed author resolution for\nchannel posts (no \"from\" field — author is the channel via sender_chat/chat)\nand added chat_id filtering in searchChannelByHandle so results are scoped\nto the target channel when the bot is in multiple chats.\n\nAuditService: record() reads organisationId/userId from the request-scoped\nRequestContext bean, which is not available on the async search thread pool.\nSearchService already captures orgId and userId before handing off to the\nasync executor. Added an explicit overload record(action, detail, orgId, userId)\nfor async callers and updated the three SearchService call sites in\nexecuteSearch/handleAsyncFailure to use it.","tree":{"sha":"0e0f8fbcc5776897095ceeb87570f0ef7e24ceab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/git/trees/0e0f8fbcc5776897095ceeb87570f0ef7e24ceab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/git/commits/b51d51bba3dc08e122bbd52d6cb2052b92148ebd","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e0f8fbcc5776897095ceeb87570f0ef7e24ceab\nparent d1cbbb6091ff1e249ee3c36f763a1e6ff71b6ec2\nauthor Shane P <shane@argodevops.co.uk> 1779297893 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779297893 +0100\n\nfix: resolve user-ui and admin-ui local-dev and Docker setup issues (#30)\n\n* fix: resolve user-ui and admin-ui local-dev and Docker issues\n\nDockerfile static assets (both UIs):\n  outputFileTracingRoot points to the monorepo root, so the standalone\n  build mirrors the full tree and server.js lands at ./user-ui/server.js.\n  Static files must be at ./user-ui/.next/static (not ./.next/static) or\n  the browser gets 404s for all CSS/JS assets.\n\n.env.example — Keycloak URLs now uncommented with local-dev defaults:\n  KEYCLOAK_EXTERNAL_URL / KEYCLOAK_INTERNAL_URL were missing entirely,\n  causing buildAuthOptions() to crash with \"Invalid URL: undefined/...\"\n  on first request. Also unblock NEXTAUTH_USER_UI_URL, NEXTAUTH_ADMIN_UI_URL,\n  KEYCLOAK_USER_UI_SECRET, KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_UI_SECRET with their dev defaults.\n\nstart-debug.sh — per-service Keycloak client IDs:\n  user-ui and admin-ui use different Keycloak clients (spider-user-ui /\n  spider-admin-ui). Inline the client-specific env vars before each npm\n  run dev invocation so both UIs get the right credentials without\n  conflicting through the shared .env.\n\nadmin-ui forbidden page:\n  Replace the static \"contact your administrator\" text with a\n  \"Copy my email address\" button so non-admin users can easily share\n  their account email when requesting access.\n\n* docs: add gotcha for start-debug.sh blank screen / Invalid URL after first setup\n\n* fix: web search returns no results; Pact tests fail with H2 seeds\n\nWebSearchAdapter: DuckDuckGo HTML endpoint silently redirects to its\nhomepage when sent a non-browser User-Agent or missing Accept headers.\nJsoup was sending only the Spider bot UA; added Accept and Accept-Language\nheaders matching a standard browser request so actual results are returned.\n\nPact provider tests: application.yml now defaults flyway.locations to\ninclude db/seed/h2, causing both @SpringBootTest-based provider tests to\nrun the V1000 seed which renames the Acme org and breaks the\nadminLicenseExists interaction. Added spring.flyway.locations=classpath:db/migration\nto both provider test @SpringBootTest properties.\n\ntest.sh: added _pact_report() to show per-interaction pass/fail after\nprovider verification, even when the step fails.\n\n* fix: Telegram returns no results for channel posts; audit fails in async thread\n\nTelegramAdapter: Telegram sends channel posts as \"channel_post\" in the\nupdate object, not \"message\". The adapter only checked update.get(\"message\")\nso every channel post was silently skipped. Fixed to fall back to\n\"channel_post\" when \"message\" is absent. Also fixed author resolution for\nchannel posts (no \"from\" field — author is the channel via sender_chat/chat)\nand added chat_id filtering in searchChannelByHandle so results are scoped\nto the target channel when the bot is in multiple chats.\n\nAuditService: record() reads organisationId/userId from the request-scoped\nRequestContext bean, which is not available on the async search thread pool.\nSearchService already captures orgId and userId before handing off to the\nasync executor. Added an explicit overload record(action, detail, orgId, userId)\nfor async callers and updated the three SearchService call sites in\nexecuteSearch/handleAsyncFailure to use it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDe5lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAclcQAErFuDykkIsHYP+8+mySoWma\ny202PSVIRPoxERuesxjAnHboJpYBd8lJ7aC6gpU96QaeEaAHsG6SYKU1XA9+I2CO\nh77tiKXcKUTBFarYesRfs41O+NeXGL1HDz1m5GWVA3kWebNSeYFjRHOcpnvgTmH8\nB611gons4lhjZKQ+iFIvj9eATibr7aL/Brj/W8DIKZt5V4cFwgdq4hPkqhftN7rU\nEt6MlBsT0PmqG51C9+CLpZwEtao7pQNMXoyXi7st58bGTj9tBkf1wx1z/pWDB9uC\nnHf1L8PdfQ5pPNrxU6LfnJKnVVKyzhzusA8BrWpqQ+F+p48t4h3/5ec43Jq+8FWY\nms97PRiDUbuiIdZnOG9C/z0/6/Fe/OUZsa7N2AL4PZhLONCjCObCC/wS+qMquoIL\n2bizpZrkVR5NKyrT5NWNKUfVjP/D9ofL+lm4si/h1Vb4gPlYtAPuB/LeSxZcPz/t\nZY3qEXgw6IAnl6XiHzpO50wFp8oZsOH79GBJeW6vmGq4O1g6UAkEyY+Jx8yV38hO\no3vPhg7nTwy4v8agmt13nfzF5yOEFeGVCEIKpApF9HlYbTrHKBqHorNkbPW7xrFB\ni0eui8SHUw6Od1TbUUihl3vgFp7Gf8c6rvaW1Rc3SSubGmSW5kYrHwOX/+rJg/wM\nTgsB+N+sudJv5GkWWHBX\n=5ju7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-29T15:47:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commit/b51d51bba3dc08e122bbd52d6cb2052b92148ebd","node_id":"C_kwDOSrf_edoAKGI1MWQ1MWJiYTNkYzA4ZTEyMmJiZDUyZDZjYjIwNTJiOTIxNDhlYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commit/d1cbbb6091ff1e249ee3c36f763a1e6ff71b6ec2","sha":"d1cbbb6091ff1e249ee3c36f763a1e6ff71b6ec2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/d1cbbb6091ff1e249ee3c36f763a1e6ff71b6ec2"}],"sha":"b51d51bba3dc08e122bbd52d6cb2052b92148ebd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/b51d51bba3dc08e122bbd52d6cb2052b92148ebd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6948843?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shanepreater","id":6948843,"login":"shanepreater","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDg4NDM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanepreater","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/commits/d1cbbb6091ff1e249ee3c36f763a1e6ff71b6ec2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-20T17:07:16Z","email":"shane@argodevops.co.uk","name":"Shane P"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-20T17:07:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: pin Pact provider tests to migration-only Flyway locations (#29)\n\n* fix: pin Pact provider tests to migration-only Flyway locations\n\napplication.yml now defaults flyway.locations to include db/seed/h2,\nwhich caused provider verification tests to run V1000 and rename\n''Acme Intelligence'' to ''Acme'', breaking the adminLicenseExists Pact\ninteraction that expects the V7 org name.\n\nFix: explicitly set spring.flyway.locations=classpath:db/migration in\nboth provider @SpringBootTest annotations so seeds never run in tests.\n\n* feat: add per-interaction Pact results summary to test.sh contracts step\n\nProvider verification results were silently swallowed by Gradle -q mode,\nmaking it impossible to tell which interactions passed or failed without\ndigging into XML reports manually.\n\nNow _pact_report() parses build/test-results XML after every provider run\nand prints a ✓/✗ table of all interactions plus a total count. The report\nruns even when the provider step fails so you can immediately see which\nspecific interactions broke.","tree":{"sha":"227a837e15f4c8ec9c2b700ebe3c560a057c8694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/git/trees/227a837e15f4c8ec9c2b700ebe3c560a057c8694"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Rsam1993/spider-monorepo/git/commits/d1cbbb6091ff1e249ee3c36f763a1e6ff71b6ec2","verification":{"payload":"tree 227a837e15f4c8ec9c2b700ebe3c560a057c8694\nparent 16012523c9c8166eca7872c2f0c759964a2cf26b\nauthor Shane P <shane@argodevops.co.uk> 1779296836 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779296836 +0100\n\nfix: pin Pact provider tests to migration-only Flyway locations (#29)\n\n* fix: pin Pact provider tests to migration-only Flyway locations\n\napplication.yml now defaults flyway.locations to include db/seed/h2,\nwhich caused provider verification tests to run V1000 and rename\n''Acme Intelligence'' to ''Acme'', breaking the adminLicenseExists Pact\ninteraction that expects the V7 org name.\n\nFix: explicitly set spring.flyway.locations=classpath:db/migration in\nboth provider @SpringBootTest annotations so seeds never run in tests.\n\n* feat: add per-interaction Pact results summary to test.sh contracts step\n\nProvider verification results were silently swallowed by Gradle -q mode,\nmaking it impossible to tell which interactions passed or failed without\ndigging into XML reports manually.\n\nNow _pact_report() parses build/test-results XML after every provider run\nand prints a ✓/✗ table of all interactions plus a total count. The report\nruns even when the provider step fails so you can immediately see which\nspecific interactions broke.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDepECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAZwQAEpSltDByNEiKDQhq0E5WJxP\njaH6yKMh+yYCrJcC+AeHSFLtCQolo8FMXrIjtXOxmdQTmIBEEgxdoE0+p80qnpa1\nBQkVcDwOmNO6/KEedrFS8oNwyR2gIn38GJEEFOmXssVN2witO9Mtx0lJkferzXKY\ngyz2pC6YN1Fhup5zhyaMCjK7Czf/vDbn5h4MAwIARlPhZ5p1jr4xOn6BT04QnQtO\nocp7DFpyrVZ3k9GD6ucYfSWYoT6IdNxaeZxE4eQe6nop9g27CWvmtj5V+CkDVg3o\njS+E6ce4RXA9UWqNK+gjkFSgTbIg3uRy5nD0iFT5iaPkgU8dbI2CUa1RTZ3XmobZ\nC4vekr1jyr+bf/2nEO4IMdkkyfBQggHUJui4UAL4W91KhDpK9vBRJO0N89wt9fTb\ncSUHqg4tlhGwKH0rkFEti6gN78xFbYa9kFbHzZv6oTSZBGivuVSTRgE8DvDvHRgW\nU73j/ZT7dftYC7AjS8/R5aNjRjmUW3Bm/b+aBQ6R3WEGZ/CZ0AckljyN0MX2i+pp\nfKzwXvq4WkN/ob+t6jB7vZjh+agpvecPgKZ9ZkW25SfmajvjZrNlRUDf9rbt8gvB\nNV+ctwRNRJ3IGBa0YU030BzCoSn2uEf/lDKtz8gqifkkZLbbxMgBYJrzXLcVB9nf\nvDVVHcsnQnRV1Sad8B1D\n=o3jM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-29T15:47:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://ava