":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/4b05bf5723bfbb6837267edde6f570268171b982/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T06:14:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T06:14:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(patterns): exclude CHANGELOG/SKILLS.md/integrations from hotspot signal\n\n/patterns flagged software-architect/references/{checklist,practices}.md as\na hotspot (4 distinct specs). Re-reviewed against the \"Simplicity and\nreversibility\" checklist (item 8.6): each touch is a small, independently\njustified cross-cutting doctrine addition with no removable duplication, so\nno /refine is needed for these files - the recurrence itself is accepted\nwith a recorded reason.\n\nThat review surfaced that CHANGELOG.md (x8) and the generated SKILLS.md /\nintegrations/** bundles (x5 each) dominate the hotspot list structurally,\nsince they''re touched by nearly every change and indicate nothing about\naccumulated complexity. scan_touched_files() now excludes them so the\nhotspot signal stays focused on areas with genuine recurring change.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Tv4HwSizQttWpyuBgK3DMM","tree":{"sha":"478a42140be6dd51810371ddc9c6e987315fa404","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/trees/478a42140be6dd51810371ddc9c6e987315fa404"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ma