servably complex logic;\n  checklist items added and the docstring/TODO items reconciled.\n- qa-engineer: checklist verifies complex logic carries tests written\n  before the implementation and flags untested complexity as a\n  release risk.\n- security-engineer: security-sensitive code is always complex\n  (test-first with negative/abuse cases); no commented-out security\n  controls; no secrets in comments.\n- software-architect: testability added as a driving quality\n  attribute (design must allow complex logic to be unit-tested in\n  isolation) and ADR discipline names the ADR as the home for design\n  rationale so code stays comment-free.\n\nSkill validator green on all four; integrations regenerated.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CNePNXuY7drAZoVJx6bjGW","tree":{"sha":"ec24d4dd3e3f8e6bade664c3604587ac705916d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/trees/ec24d4dd3e3f8e6bade664c3604587ac705916d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/commits/69efda628410e9498fe51a9c2ad472124abe1556","verification":{"payload":"tree ec24d4dd3e3f8e6bade664c3604587ac705916d3\nparent 118e381cdbc97cc7fe11e3275908c810b638c799\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1781115347 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1781115347 +0000\n\nfeat(skills): adopt team conventions — comment-free code and test-first for complex logic\n\nApplies the accepted ledger decision 20260610-181128-01db across four\nrole experts:\n\n- developer: Comments section tightened to the binding comment-free\n  rule (only constraint-stating comments; no commented-out code or\n  inline TODO/FIXME; docstrings on public APIs stay) and the TDD\n  section now mandates test-first for observably complex logic;\n  checklist items added and the docstring/TODO items reconciled.\n- qa-engineer: checklist verifies complex logic carries tests written\n  before the implementation and flags untested complexity as a\n  release risk.\n- security-engineer: security-sensitive cod