,"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Make harness mode always-on with auto-bootstrap (remove opt-in)\n\nHarness mode is now praxis''s default and only operating mode. The\n\"if not in harness mode, behave as before\" fallback is gone; a missing\n.praxis/config.json is auto-bootstrapped instead of treated as \"no harness\".\n\n- tools/ensure_harness.py (new, make harness-init): idempotent, stdlib-only\n  bootstrap. Derives a projectId from the repo name and writes config +\n  project memory — central mode under projects/<id>/ for the harness repo\n  itself, local mode under .praxis/project/ for a consuming repo. No-op once\n  initialized. Covered by tools/test_ensure_harness.py.\n- /new-feature, /fix-bug, /refine, /review-changes: drop the non-harness\n  branch; call ensure_harness first so a project always resolves.\n- Stop conditions narrowed: a missing config is not a hard block (it is\n  bootstrapped); only a present-but-broken config (malformed, or a projectId\n  that does not resolve) stops the agent — it asks rather than overwriting.\n- Doctrine + docs updated from \"opt-in / experimental\" to \"always on\":\n  AGENTS.md, rules/source-of-truth.md, rules/stop-conditions.md, README,\n  docs/harness-mode.md, docs/index.html. Integrations regenerated.\n- The praxis repo itself now carries .praxis/config.json + projects/praxis/.\n\nThis is a deliberate backward-compatibility break: consuming repos that ran\nin non-harness mode without a config now run in harness mode (bootstrapped).\n\nValidation: 113 tests, validate-harness, validate-all, catalog-check,\nintegrations-check, validate-traceability all pass.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01NjrHRKNZ5FQg7dYpxK61QZ","tree":{"sha":"81670bef29e636cbf7894c775eb677b31d5eec96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/trees/81670bef29e636cbf7894c775eb677b31d5eec96"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/commits/b77fdb03394f8698d055566a9e74a21ad0d4bdb0","verification":{"payload":"tree 81670bef29e636cbf7894c775eb677b31d5eec96\nparent 80a868620f402bc41f9bbbbfdac3705107f30d4b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1781014301 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1781014301 +0000\n\nMake harness mode always-on with auto-bootstrap (remove opt-in)\n\nHarness mode is now praxis''s default and only operating mode. The\n\"if not in harness mode, behave as before\" fallback is gone; a missing\n.praxis/config.json is auto-bootstrapped instead of treated as \"no harness\".\n\n- tools/ensure_harness.py (new, make harness-init): idempotent, stdlib-only\n  bootstrap. Derives a projectId from the repo name and writes config +\n  project memory — central mode under projects/<id>/ for the harness repo\n  itself, local mode under .praxis/project/ for a consuming repo. No-op once\n  initialized. Covered by tools/test_ensure_harness.py.\n- /new-feature, /fix-bug, /refine, /review-changes: drop the non-harness\n  branch; call ensure_harness first so a project always resolves.\n- Stop conditions narrowed: a missing config is not a hard block (it is\n  bootstrapped); only a present-but-broken config (malformed, or a projectId\n  that does not resolve) stops the agent — it asks rather than overwriting.\n- Doctrine + docs updated from \"opt-in / experimental\" to \"always on\":\n  AGENTS.md, rules/source-of-truth.md, rules/stop-conditions.md, README,\n  docs/harness-mode.md, docs/index.html. Integrations regenerated.\n- The praxis repo itself now carries .praxis/config.json + projects/praxis/.\n\nThis is a deliberate backward-compatibility break: consuming repos that ran\nin non-harness mode without a config now run in harness mode (bootstrapped).\n\nValidation: 113 tests, validate-harness, validate-all, catalog-check,\nintegrations-check, validate-traceability all pass.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01NjrHRKNZ5FQg7dYpxK61QZ\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrL