"commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T20:21:47Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T20:21:47Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"promote: don''t clobber the adjudication decision_ref\n\nAddresses PR #25 review (P2): promote.py from-assumption overwrote the\nassumption''s decision_ref — which holds the memory-ledger entry recording the\nuser''s confirm/correct adjudication — with the pending promotion proposal id,\nlosing the durable link to the decision that validated the assumption.\n\n- Add a distinct `promotion_ref` field on the assumption (schema + tool).\n- _link_assumption now writes promotion_ref and never touches decision_ref.\n- tests: assert decision_ref set via `confirm --decision` survives a promotion\n  and the proposal id lands in promotion_ref (suite now 67).\n- never-assume.md: clarify the two distinct references.","tree":{"sha":"583044e388de033804a594597eb0dbb925fba2b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/trees/583044e388de033804a594597eb0dbb925fba2b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/commits/013955f6164606fa5c864ea06392638efa16f50b","verification":{"payload":"tree 583044e388de033804a594597eb0dbb925fba2b9\nparent 70d11c66547fb08f39fcefc2a85b0f81e3f38e22\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780950107 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780950107 +0000\n\npromote: don''t clobber the adjudication decision_ref\n\nAddresses PR #25 review (P2): promote.py from-assumption overwrote the\nassumption''s decision_ref — which holds the memory-ledger entry recording the\nuser''s confirm/correct adjudication — with the pending promotion proposal id,\nlosing the durable link to the decision that validated the assumption.\n\n- Add a distinct `promotion_ref` field on the assumption (schema + tool).\n- _link_assumption now writes promotion_ref and never touches decision_ref.\n- tests: assert decision_ref set via `confirm --decision` survives a promotion\n  and the proposal id lands in promotion_ref (suite now 67).\n- never-assume.md: clarify the two distinct references.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFqqw1zC\nspG9XgCJNLBLDlycGLTsaYvpgoWfnHUb5J01es9bNNFBmD+M5FbHcYC4n1DTdC0YP95Bm3rN0xjM\nlQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-08T20:21:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/013955f6164606fa5c864ea06392638efa16f50b","node_id":"C_kwDOSroCA9oAKDAxMzk1NWY2MTY0NjA2ZmE1Yzg2NGVhMDYzOTI2MzhlZmExNmY1MGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/70d11c66547fb08f39fcefc2a85b0f81e3f38e22","sha":"70d11c66547fb08f39fcefc2a85b0f81e3f38e22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/70d11c66547fb08f39fcefc2a85b0f81e3f38e22"}],"sha":"013955f6164606fa5c864ea06392638efa16f50b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/013955f6164606fa5c864ea06392638efa16f50b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/70d11c66547fb08f39fcefc2a85b0f81e3f38e22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T19:56:58Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T19:56:58Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add promotion executor: close the learning loop, human-gated\n\nA validated assumption (or an evidenced gap) can become durable governance —\na rule, gate, eval, or guardrail. This adds the deterministic, human-gated\nbridge from a resolved decision to a pending governance proposal.\n\n- tools/promote.py: the executor. `from-assumption` (requires the assumption\n  be confirmed/corrected — promote on evidence, never anticipation) and\n  `propose` (direct, evidence required) record a PENDING `decision` in the\n  memory ledger, tagged promotion / promote:<target> / source:<ASSUME-id>,\n  with the evidence chain, a draft slot, and per-target authoring routing.\n  It never writes rules/ or workflows/ — propose, never mutate. Plus\n  `list` and `routing`. Reuses assumptions.py + the memory ledger; adds no\n  new state.\n- tools/test_promote.py: 13 tests (suite now 66), incl. the evidence gate\n  and the assumption<->proposal linkage.\n- .claude/skills/skill-learner/workflows/promote-governance.md: the human\n  judgement around the executor; SKILL.md gains the workflow row (frontmatter\n  untouched, so the trigger surface is unchanged).\n- rules/never-assume.md: the promotion section now names promote.py as the\n  only sanctioned path and spells out the two enforced rules.\n- AGENTS.md: list promote.py in the harness tools.","tree":{"sha":"0f7219f9be86b7a3b2e030cd577cb3dbbc6280a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/trees/0f7219f9be86b7a3b2e030cd577cb3dbbc6280a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/commits/70d11c66547fb08f39fcefc2a85b0f81e3f38e22","verification":{"payload":"tree 0f7219f9be86b7a3b2e030cd577cb3dbbc6280a3\nparent ebc7a2fa41e35831fde7615ebf5481942760a49c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780948618 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780948618 +0000\n\nAdd promotion executor: close the learning loop, human-gated\n\nA validated assumption (or an evidenced gap) can become durable governance —\na rule, gate, eval, or guardrail. This adds the deterministic, human-gated\nbridge from a resolved decision to a pending governance proposal.\n\n- tools/promote.py: the executor. `from-assumption` (requires the assumption\n  be confirmed/corrected — promote on evidence, never anticipation) and\n  `propose` (direct, evidence required) record a PENDING `decision` in the\n  memory ledger, tagged promotion / promote:<target> / source:<ASSUME-id>,\n  with the evidence chain, a draft slot, and per-target authoring routing.\n  It never writes rules/ or workflows/ — propose, never mutate. Plus\n  `list` and `routing`. Reuses assumptions.py + the memory ledger; adds no\n  new state.\n- tools/test_promote.py: 13 tests (suite now 66), incl. the evidence gate\n  and the assumption<->proposal linkage.\n- .claude/skills/skill-learner/workflows/promote-governance.md: the human\n  judgement around the executor; SKILL.md gains the workflow row (frontmatter\n  untouched, so the trigger surface is unchanged).\n- rules/never-assume.md: the promotion section now names promote.py as the\n  only sanctioned path and spells out the two enforced rules.\n- AGENTS.md: list promote.py in the harness tools.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF2vccYc\n4yTrOM+SHmm7eT71bqMsnARDzLaa2+xiURzcNFpjIlEvhbBdr8DJY1O5wIPOpqfj3tdAIRsmAU4X\nMQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-08T19:57:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/70d11c66547fb08f39fcefc2a85b0f81e3f38e22","node_id":"C_kwDOSroCA9oAKDcwZDExYzY2NTQ3ZmIwOGYzOWZjZWZjMmE4NWIwZjgxZTNmMzhlMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/ebc7a2fa41e35831fde7615ebf5481942760a49c","sha":"ebc7a2fa41e35831fde7615ebf5481942760a49c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/ebc7a2fa41e35831fde7615ebf5481942760a49c"}],"sha":"70d11c66547fb08f39fcefc2a85b0f81e3f38e22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/70d11c66547fb08f39fcefc2a85b0f81e3f38e22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/ebc7a2fa41e35831fde7615ebf5481942760a49c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T19:46:31Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T19:46:31Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Make assumptions & loop validation ambient via opt-in hooks\n\nSlices 1-3 added the tools and wired loop-control into the lifecycles, but\nthey only fired when invoked by hand. This surfaces them automatically.\n\n- integrations/hooks/validation.settings.example.json: opt-in template.\n  SessionStart surfaces open assumptions (`assumptions.py open --brief`)\n  and escalated/running loops (`loop.py brief`) into context; a PreToolUse\n  nudge re-surfaces them before a commit/push. Nudges only (exit 0), silent\n  when nothing is open. Resolves the harness tools/ dir from the consuming\n  repo''s .praxis/config.json harnessRoot, falling back to $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\n  for harness self-dev — verified end-to-end against a simulated consumer.\n- tools/loop.py: add `brief` (compact escalated/running summary for hooks).\n- tools/test_loop.py: 3 tests for brief (suite now 53).\n- rules/never-assume.md, rules/loop-control.md: document the ambient hook.\n- integrations/README.md: new \"Ambient validation\" section (+ table row).\n- AGENTS.md: note the validation template in the directory map.\n\npraxis ships the template and does not enable it on itself.","tree":{"sha":"a0bb34fbb4b71549d1e984146f975d3ad6cc0ded","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/trees/a0bb34fbb4b71549d1e984146f975d3ad6cc0ded"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/commits/ebc7a2fa41e35831fde7615ebf5481942760a49c","verification":{"payload":"tree a0bb34fbb4b71549d1e984146f975d3ad6cc0ded\nparent 196837366e8ad08ea94f0b0e7c905d46df908c94\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780947991 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780947991 +0000\n\nMake assumptions & loop validation ambient via opt-in hooks\n\nSlices 1-3 added the tools and wired loop-control into the lifecycles, but\nthey only fired when invoked by hand. This surfaces them automatically.\n\n- integrations/hooks/validation.settings.example.json: opt-in template.\n  SessionStart surfaces open assumptions (`assumptions.py open --brief`)\n  and escalated/running loops (`loop.py brief`) into context; a PreToolUse\n  nudge re-surfaces them before a commit/push. Nudges only (exit 0), silent\n  when nothing is open. Resolves the harness tools/ dir from the consuming\n  repo''s .praxis/config.json harnessRoot, falling back to $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\n  for harness self-dev — verified end-to-end against a simulated consumer.\n- tools/loop.py: add `brief` (compact escalated/running summary for hooks).\n- tools/test_loop.py: 3 tests for brief (suite now 53).\n- rules/never-assume.md, rules/loop-control.md: document the ambient hook.\n- integrations/README.md: new \"Ambient validation\" section (+ table row).\n- AGENTS.md: note the validation template in the directory map.\n\npraxis ships the template and does not enable it on itself.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMhQ5iVi\nJSTUHzQQYzgmGpo7WRVuadF7+AZ6Tzah00VvD/S5APlHZ7dEKuvQ3wjT6JW+/vJZDJGErM25sjiY\nJQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-08T19:46:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/ebc7a2fa41e35831fde7615ebf5481942760a49c","node_id":"C_kwDOSroCA9oAKGViYzdhMmZhNDFlMzU4MzFmZGU3NjE1ZWJmNTQ4MTk0Mjc2MGE0OWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/196837366e8ad08ea94f0b0e7c905d46df908c94","sha":"196837366e8ad08ea94f0b0e7c905d46df908c94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/196837366e8ad08ea94f0b0e7c905d46df908c94"}],"sha":"ebc7a2fa41e35831fde7615ebf5481942760a49c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/ebc7a2fa41e35831fde7615ebf5481942760a49c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/196837366e8ad08ea94f0b0e7c905d46df908c94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T19:31:33Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T19:31:33Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Wire loop-control into the workflow lifecycles\n\nMakes the convergence loop enforced by the lifecycle, not just available:\nthe verify step (and corrective fix→verify / change→verify) now carries a\nmachine-readable terminal predicate and guards.\n\n- schemas/workflow.schema.json: add the optional `loops` block — per-step\n  predicate (non-empty), maxIterations/patience guards, and onContinue\n  (the step to return to on a `continue` verdict, e.g. verify→build).\n- tools/validate_harness.py: validate `loops` — keys must be steps, the\n  predicate must be non-empty, guards positive integers, onContinue a\n  real step. New _check_workflow_loops helper.\n- workflows/{feature-development,bug-fix,refinement}.workflow.json:\n  declare loops.verify with each lifecycle''s acceptance predicate and its\n  back-edge (build / fix / change).\n- systems/: document the verify convergence loop in the feature-development\n  doctrine and the bug-fix / refinement artifact models.\n- tools/test_harness_tools.py: 5 tests for the loops validation (suite 50).\n- AGENTS.md: note the convergence loop on the workflows entry.","tree":{"sha":"0f329fdbbd487d25b359f1714a6791c7799b5f88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/trees/0f329fdbbd487d25b359f1714a6791c7799b5f88"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/commits/196837366e8ad08ea94f0b0e7c905d46df908c94","verification":{"payload":"tree 0f329fdbbd487d25b359f1714a6791c7799b5f88\nparent f5840f34156b454c9cde0217f4988b795db51bfe\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780947093 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780947093 +0000\n\nWire loop-control into the workflow lifecycles\n\nMakes the convergence loop enforced by the lifecycle, not just available:\nthe verify step (and corrective fix→verify / change→verify) now carries a\nmachine-readable terminal predicate and guards.\n\n- schemas/workflow.schema.json: add the optional `loops` block — per-step\n  predicate (non-empty), maxIterations/patience guards, and onContinue\n  (the step to return to on a `continue` verdict, e.g. verify→build).\n- tools/validate_harness.py: validate `loops` — keys must be steps, the\n  predicate must be non-empty, guards positive integers, onContinue a\n  real step. New _check_workflow_loops helper.\n- workflows/{feature-development,bug-fix,refinement}.workflow.json:\n  declare loops.verify with each lifecycle''s acceptance predicate and its\n  back-edge (build / fix / change).\n- systems/: document the verify convergence loop in the feature-development\n  doctrine and the bug-fix / refinement artifact models.\n- tools/test_harness_tools.py: 5 tests for the loops validation (suite 50).\n- AGENTS.md: note the convergence loop on the workflows entry.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEpQUKiY\n3MqY6ieMGrI5YvtSr1g1UMJvhO2Aijii5Ad5SF73irliUIocOnvB53iVN/qZJ5pjOmml83XqprBh\nmwQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-08T19:31:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/196837366e8ad08ea94f0b0e7c905d46df908c94","node_id":"C_kwDOSroCA9oAKDE5NjgzNzM2NmU4YWQwOGVhOTRmMGIwZTdjOTA1ZDQ2ZGY5MDhjOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/f5840f34156b454c9cde0217f4988b795db51bfe","sha":"f5840f34156b454c9cde0217f4988b795db51bfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/f5840f34156b454c9cde0217f4988b795db51bfe"}],"sha":"196837366e8ad08ea94f0b0e7c905d46df908c94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/196837366e8ad08ea94f0b0e7c905d46df908c94"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/f5840f34156b454c9cde0217f4988b795db51bfe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T18:29:30Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T18:29:30Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add loop controller: bounded \"loop until correct\"\n\nCloses the never-ending-loop gap. A build → verify → fix loop now runs\nagainst an explicit terminal predicate under two guards, so it converges\nor escalates but never spins.\n\n- rules/loop-control.md: the harness rule. Completes the trio with\n  stop-conditions (stop & ask) and never-assume (log & validate): this\n  governs the \"keep iterating, but bounded\" lane. A loop must declare a\n  terminal predicate (non-empty acceptance criteria) and a budget; each\n  iteration yields a closed-set verdict (continue/done/escalate);\n  escalate is a real stop handed to the user, not a silent budget bump.\n- tools/loop.py: stdlib-only CLI. start / tick / resume / resolve /\n  status / list / show. `tick` computes the verdict deterministically —\n  done > budget-exhausted > no-progress > continue — with no-progress\n  detected via an unchanging (criteria-met-count + signal) signature.\n- tools/test_loop.py: 16 tests (picked up by `make test`; suite now 45).\n- schemas/loop.schema.json: closed status/verdict sets, typed LOOP- id,\n  non-empty predicate enforced.\n- AGENTS.md: wire the rule, tool, and schema into the harness doctrine.","tree":{"sha":"d926a73cb29c61c03aaa46d871e7d5b6e469d354","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/trees/d926a73cb29c61c03aaa46d871e7d5b6e469d354"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/commits/f5840f34156b454c9cde0217f4988b795db51bfe","verification":{"payload":"tree d926a73cb29c61c03aaa46d871e7d5b6e469d354\nparent 5054ec38c2f46ce33cb033bd3ab3d031f42d5cfd\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780943370 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780943370 +0000\n\nAdd loop controller: bounded \"loop until correct\"\n\nCloses the never-ending-loop gap. A build → verify → fix loop now runs\nagainst an explicit terminal predicate under two guards, so it converges\nor escalates but never spins.\n\n- rules/loop-control.md: the harness rule. Completes the trio with\n  stop-conditions (stop & ask) and never-assume (log & validate): this\n  governs the \"keep iterating, but bounded\" lane. A loop must declare a\n  terminal predicate (non-empty acceptance criteria) and a budget; each\n  iteration yields a closed-set verdict (continue/done/escalate);\n  escalate is a real stop handed to the user, not a silent budget bump.\n- tools/loop.py: stdlib-only CLI. start / tick / resume / resolve /\n  status / list / show. `tick` computes the verdict deterministically —\n  done > budget-exhausted > no-progress > continue — with no-progress\n  detected via an unchanging (criteria-met-count + signal) signature.\n- tools/test_loop.py: 16 tests (picked up by `make test`; suite now 45).\n- schemas/loop.schema.json: closed status/verdict sets, typed LOOP- id,\n  non-empty predicate enforced.\n- AGENTS.md: wire the rule, tool, and schema into the harness doctrine.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIST+Ira\nnWiTnjTWD+22KHWwig4da28IpNd+3CbkLWzC4CWXrBMywIZMe/PtlAC+7B30wU/QTNFCRnsU9gmr\njA4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-08T18:29:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/f5840f34156b454c9cde0217f4988b795db51bfe","node_id":"C_kwDOSroCA9oAKGY1ODQwZjM0MTU2YjQ1NGM5Y2RlMDIxN2Y0OTg4Yjc5NWRiNTFiZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/5054ec38c2f46ce33cb033bd3ab3d031f42d5cfd","sha":"5054ec38c2f46ce33cb033bd3ab3d031f42d5cfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/5054ec38c2f46ce33cb033bd3ab3d031f42d5cfd"}],"sha":"f5840f34156b454c9cde0217f4988b795db51bfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/f5840f34156b454c9cde0217f4988b795db51bfe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/5054ec38c2f46ce33cb033bd3ab3d031f42d5cfd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T17:53:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T17:53:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add assumptions ledger: \"never assume, always validate\"\n\nIntroduces the deterministic spine of the rule by the same name — the\nkeystone of spec-driven, loop-until-correct work.\n\n- rules/never-assume.md: the harness rule. High confidence → assert;\n  material ambiguity → stop (per stop-conditions); low-stakes/reversible\n  uncertainty → log an assumption and proceed. Resolution → decision →\n  human-gated, pending promotion to a rule/guardrail/eval/gate.\n- tools/assumptions.py: stdlib-only CLI mirroring the memory ledger.\n  add / list / open / show / sweep / confirm / correct / withdraw / status.\n  `sweep` deterministically renders open assumptions as an A/B/C\n  question-flow, lowest-confidence-first, recommended answer = what was\n  assumed, free-form always allowed.\n- tools/test_assumptions.py: 12 tests (picked up by `make test`).\n- schemas/assumption.schema.json: closed status set, typed ASSUME- id.\n- AGENTS.md: wire the rule, tool, and schema into the harness doctrine.","tree":{"sha":"a3878f7def05efc0236c88d7b7a3cd5db5839b1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/trees/a3878f7def05efc0236c88d7b7a3cd5db5839b1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/commits/5054ec38c2f46ce33cb033bd3ab3d031f42d5cfd","verification":{"payload":"tree a3878f7def05efc0236c88d7b7a3cd5db5839b1f\nparent fa4b9ff38b044051286fa0359ab409cbeb61c092\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780941222 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780941222 +0000\n\nAdd assumptions ledger: \"never assume, always validate\"\n\nIntroduces the deterministic spine of the rule by the same name — the\nkeystone of spec-driven, loop-until-correct work.\n\n- rules/never-assume.md: the harness rule. High confidence → assert;\n  material ambiguity → stop (per stop-conditions); low-stakes/reversible\n  uncertainty → log an assumption and proceed. Resolution → decision →\n  human-gated, pending promotion to a rule/guardrail/eval/gate.\n- tools/assumptions.py: stdlib-only CLI mirroring the memory ledger.\n  add / list / open / show / sweep / confirm / correct / withdraw / status.\n  `sweep` deterministically renders open assumptions as an A/B/C\n  question-flow, lowest-confidence-first, recommended answer = what was\n  assumed, free-form always allowed.\n- tools/test_assumptions.py: 12 tests (picked up by `make test`).\n- schemas/assumption.schema.json: closed status set, typed ASSUME- id.\n- AGENTS.md: wire the rule, tool, and schema into the harness doctrine.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGYfoVcT\ngDYbrpR7wuymCjC5w6XBNFrTRdJByAkm3xoDHAaXJadRLEINvqjFjALlIh6SS5fNr49ZBvgK65Bw\ngwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-08T17:53:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/5054ec38c2f46ce33cb033bd3ab3d031f42d5cfd","node_id":"C_kwDOSroCA9oAKDUwNTRlYzM4YzJmNDZjZTMzY2IwMzNiZDNhYjNkMDMxZjQyZDVjZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/fa4b9ff38b044051286fa0359ab409cbeb61c092","sha":"fa4b9ff38b044051286fa0359ab409cbeb61c092","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/fa4b9ff38b044051286fa0359ab409cbeb61c092"}],"sha":"5054ec38c2f46ce33cb033bd3ab3d031f42d5cfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/