orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/08cc3c5c523e6c0d32da38186d3bdb2e2eec5be2","node_id":"C_kwDOSroCA9oAKDA4Y2MzYzVjNTIzZTZjMGQzMmRhMzgxODZkM2JkYjJlMmVlYzViZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/18b287e43af1d51516446465853dbeb2469a4de2","sha":"18b287e43af1d51516446465853dbeb2469a4de2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/18b287e43af1d51516446465853dbeb2469a4de2"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/2ff4b64ddf633e98ca3e1e23393b7bc981f43e3c","sha":"2ff4b64ddf633e98ca3e1e23393b7bc981f43e3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/2ff4b64ddf633e98ca3e1e23393b7bc981f43e3c"}],"sha":"08cc3c5c523e6c0d32da38186d3bdb2e2eec5be2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/08cc3c5c523e6c0d32da38186d3bdb2e2eec5be2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/2ff4b64ddf633e98ca3e1e23393b7bc981f43e3c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T14:45:35Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T14:45:35Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"UX pass: a11y fixes (WCAG 2.2 AA), press states, back-to-top\n\nDesign-QA pass on the landing page in the UX/UI Engineer lens. Findings\nlabeled by severity; all WCAG 2.2 AA failures fixed.\n\nMust-fix (AA):\n- 1.1.1 Non-text Content: hide the three value-prop emoji icons from\n  assistive tech with aria-hidden (the Factory section already did this) —\n  no more \"factory, brain, electric plug\" read aloud.\n- 4.1.3 Status Messages: copy confirmation was silent to screen readers\n  (aria-label was the accessible name, so the visible text swap wasn''t\n  announced). Add a polite role=status live region and announce\n  copy success/failure.\n- 2.5.8 Target Size: give desktop nav links a 40px min-height hit area;\n  the active-section underline moves to absolute positioning so the flex\n  hit area doesn''t displace it.\n\nPolish:\n- Nielsen #1 (system status): add :active press feedback to buttons and\n  tabs (~150-300ms, natural easing; disabled under reduced-motion).\n- Nielsen #3 (user control): add an accessible back-to-top button that\n  appears after the hero, scrolls smoothly (auto under reduced-motion),\n  and returns keyboard focus to the top for a sensible tab order.\n- Add forced-colors (Windows High Contrast) support for focus, the active\n  nav indicator, surfaces and the back-to-top control, and an opaque\n  header fallback under prefers-reduced-transparency.\n- Add an .sr-only utility for visually-hidden, announced content.","tree":{"sha":"635a861a67889f29e4d17d25e604c05c20387f21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/trees/635a861a67889f29e4d17d25e604c05c20387f21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/commits/2ff4b64ddf633e98ca3e1e23393b7bc981f43e3c","verification":{"payload":"tree 635a861a67889f29e4d17d25e604c05c20387f21\nparent e07e9199d06f76079001ae653528544dcfddb05a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780757135 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780757135 +0000\n\nUX pass: a11y fixes (WCAG 2.2 AA), press states, back-to-top\n\nDesign-QA pass on the landing page in the UX/UI Engineer lens. Findings\nlabeled by severity; all WCAG 2.2 AA failures fixed.\n\nMust-fix (AA):\n- 1.1.1 Non-text Content: hide the three value-prop emoji icons from\n  assistive tech with aria-hidden (the Factory section already did this) —\n  no more \"factory, brain, electric plug\" read aloud.\n- 4.1.3 Status Messages: copy confirmation was silent to screen readers\n  (aria-label was the accessible name, so the visible text swap wasn''t\n  announced). Add a polite role=status live region and announce\n  copy success/failure.\n- 2.5.8 Target Size: give desktop nav links a 40px min-height hit area;\n  the active-section underline moves to absolute positioning so the flex\n  hit area doesn''t displace it.\n\nPolish:\n- Nielsen #1 (system status): add :active press feedback to buttons and\n  tabs (~150-300ms, natural easing; disabled under reduced-motion).\n- Nielsen #3 (user control): add an accessible back-to-top button that\n  appears after the hero, scrolls smoothly (auto under reduced-motion),\n  and returns keyboard focus to the top for a sensible tab order.\n- Add forced-colors (Windows High Contrast) support for focus, the active\n  nav indicator, surfaces and the back-to-top control, and an opaque\n  header fallback under prefers-reduced-transparency.\n- Add an .sr-only utility for visually-hidden, announced content.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDsTFBu3\nAXV/7W4EyDMLiT8SdzzslZ1ZiGYkZuf8OHsh1NXwxFSI9JMppCrsWB9xqX+g4pTyvtbWrHN9KHk5\ntQk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-06T14:45:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/2ff4b64ddf633e98ca3e1e23393b7bc981f43e3c","node_id":"C_kwDOSroCA9oAKDJmZjRiNjRkZGY2MzNlOThjYTNlMWUyMzM5M2I3YmM5ODFmNDNlM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcrabadan/praxis/commit/e07e9199d06f76079001ae653528544dcfddb05a","sha":"e07e9199d06f76079001ae653528544dcfddb05a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/e07e9199d06f76079001ae653528544dcfddb05a"}],"sha":"2ff4b64ddf633e98ca3e1e23393b7bc981f43e3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/2ff4b64ddf633e98ca3e1e23393b7bc981f43e3c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/commits/e07e9199d06f76079001ae653528544dcfddb05a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T14:17:38Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T14:17:38Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Enhance landing page: light/dark theming, scrollspy nav, structured data\n\nAdd a proper theming architecture and navigation/discovery improvements to\nthe GitHub Pages landing page, preserving the zero-build, zero-dependency,\nWCAG-AA and reduced-motion constraints.\n\n- Theming: introduce a light theme alongside the existing dark one. Split\n  the accent token into a brand fill (--accent) and a text/link variant\n  (--accent-ink) that darkens for AA contrast on light surfaces. Terminal\n  and code panels are pinned to fixed dark tokens so they keep their\n  intended look in both themes. A header toggle persists the choice to\n  localStorage and otherwise follows prefers-color-scheme; an inline\n  bootstrap sets the theme before paint to avoid a flash, and theme-color\n  is kept in sync.\n- Navigation: IntersectionObserver scrollspy marks the active section on\n  desktop and mobile nav links via aria-current, with a subtle underline.\n- Discovery: add JSON-LD (WebSite + SoftwareSourceCode) structured data.\n- Polish: animate the mobile hamburger into a close icon.","tree":{"sha":"c00f8c43b632e04bfba6c9df658eefbc6765403f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/trees/c00f8c43b632e04bfba6c9df658eefbc6765403f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcrabadan/praxis/git/commits/e07e9199d06f76079001ae653528544dcfddb05a","verification":{"payload":"tree c00f8c43b632e04bfba6c9df658eefbc6765403f\nparent 18b287e43af1d51516446465853dbeb2469a4de2\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780755458 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780755458 +0000\n\nEnhance landing page: light/dark theming, scrollspy nav, structured data\n\nAdd a proper theming architecture and navigation/discovery improvements to\nthe GitHub Pages landing page, preserving the zero-build, zero-dependency,\nWCAG-AA and reduced-motion constraints.\n\n- Theming: introduce a light theme alongside the existing dark one. Split\n  the accent token into a brand fill (--accent) and a text/link variant\n  (--accent-ink) that darkens for AA contrast on light surfaces. Terminal\n  and code panels are pinned to fixed dark tokens so they keep their\n  intended look in both themes. A header toggle persists the choice to\n  localStorage and otherwise follows prefers-color-scheme; an inline\n  bootstrap sets the theme before paint to avoid a flash, and theme-color\n  is kept in sync.\n- Navigation: IntersectionObserver scrollspy marks the active section on\n  desktop and mobile nav links via aria-current, with a subtle underline.\n- Discovery: add JSON-LD (WebSite + SoftwareSourceCode) structured data.\n- Polish: animate the mobile hamburger into a close icon.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOIrAtSe\n