,"site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heilashahidi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heilashahidi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/heilashahidi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/heilashahidi/weekly-commit-module/commits/de848f49a62be39026041aa78451092eee5dc425/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T20:02:49Z","email":"heila.shahidi@gmail.com","name":"Heila Shahidi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T20:02:49Z","email":"heila.shahidi@gmail.com","name":"Heila Shahidi"},"message":"refactor(lifecycle): extract OwnedPlanLoader + scalar count queries\n\nFrom the /simplify pass (unanimous across 4 review angles):\n- Extract OwnedPlanLoader (@Component) consolidating the load-plan-or-404 +\n  ownership-403 logic that was copy-pasted verbatim across 5 services, plus\n  loadCommitment (404) and requireStatus (409). One place owns the plan-access\n  policy; injected in place of the repeated repo+resolver pairs. ManagerReview\n  deliberately keeps its existence-only check (any principal may review).\n- Add countByWeeklyPlanId / existsByWeeklyPlanId and use them on the latency\n  path (LifecycleService.toDto/lock, backstop auto-lock) instead of hydrating\n  the full commitment list just to count/check-empty (PRD <200ms target).\n\nBehavior-preserving; full ./gradlew check green (132 lifecycle tests, JaCoCo 80%).\nKept the LEGAL_TRANSITIONS map, explicit sweep blocks, and ManagerReview.reviewer\ncolumn (skipped those findings with rationale).","tree":{"sha":"8ee2abd8a32d8af588c6cc4055930441cbfc4df5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/heilashahidi/weekly-commit-module/git/trees/8ee2abd8a32d8af588c6cc4055930441cbfc4df5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/heilashahidi/weekly-commit-module/git/commits/de848f49a62be39026041aa78451092eee5dc425","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":