s://api.github.com/users/shmul95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmul95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shmul95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hanjing06/permitflow/commits/f6691753ffd963416ce2cd408516cc51dbb4e7c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-31T05:28:56Z","email":"samuel.gross@epitech.eu","name":"shmul95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-31T05:28:56Z","email":"samuel.gross@epitech.eu","name":"shmul95"},"message":"feat(08-01): emit normalized_street + direction + geo_id from permit constructors\n\n- _permit_from_open_toronto (anchors): adds normalized_street/direction/geo_id;\n  street_name display field preserved verbatim (Phase 4 frontend reads it).\n- _permit_from_simple_csv: now dispatches by schema:\n    * utility_cuts.csv  → DISPLAY_DESC + PROPOSED_FROM/TO_DATE + GEO_ID\n    * building_permits.csv → composed STREET_DIRECTION/NAME/TYPE + GEO_ID\n    * legacy permits.csv → unchanged simple path\n  Schemas 1 and 2 still return None when lat/lon absent — preserves the\n  documented silent-drop behaviour for the v1.0 demo.\n- New _coerce_geo_id helper stringifies CSV float GEO_IDs (drops trailing .0).\n- New backend/tests/test_optimizer_loaders.py: 6 tests covering all three\n  schemas + the _coerce_geo_id edge cases; all green.\n- Confirmed: load_canonical_permits() yields 532 permits, 307 distinct\n  normalized_street values — same volume as v1.0 baseline.","tree":{"sha":"60af8b56c453c11225b4f869d1168814a6dec296","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hanjing06/permitflow/git/trees/60af8b56c453c11225b4f869d1168814a6dec296"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hanjing06/permitflow/git/commits/f6691753ffd963416ce2cd408516cc51dbb4e7c6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146193617?v=4","e