:"https://api.github.com/users/shmul95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hanjing06/permitflow/commits/462a44bd90d800e38770d3420e2ca3c7a630b999/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-31T03:08:15Z","email":"samuel.gross@epitech.eu","name":"shmul95"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-31T03:08:15Z","email":"samuel.gross@epitech.eu","name":"shmul95"},"message":"phase(08): add street-based clustering as a v1.1 post-hackathon roadmap entry\n\nCaptured during v1.0 hackathon as a follow-up improvement to the\noptimizer. Not in v1.0 scope (frozen at hour 35 per D-74).\n\nThe current radius-based DBSCAN in cluster_leftover_candidates has two\nhonest failure modes:\n- false positives: clusters permits on parallel streets that share no\n  trench (220m radius doesn''t know about street topology)\n- false negatives: misses permits on the same street more than 220m\n  apart that DO share a trench (literally the trench-sharing thesis)\n\nPhase 8 captures a three-layer fix (same-street normalized name →\nGEO_ID exact match → cross-street intersection tag). Each layer is\nshippable independently. Expected lift: 2x-5x more clusters with no\ndata changes.\n\nROADMAP.md gets a Phase 8 checkbox + a detailed section explaining\nscope, caveats, and the v1.1-milestone deferral.\n08-CONTEXT.md captures the thesis, three-layer breakdown, data\nmodel changes, and dependencies for the eventual planner pass.\n\nAlso fixed the auto-generated phase slug which got truncated\nmid-word: ''08-street-based-clustering-replace-radius-based-dbscan-\nwith-sam'' → ''08-street-based-clustering''. Directory renamed (was\nempty so no git tracking impact).","tree":{"sha":"4b3f977943dcd82332e59c2d3cfc8fcd1187d398","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hanjing06/permitflow/git/trees/4b3f977943dcd82332e59c2d3cfc8fcd1187d398"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hanjing06/permitflow/git/commits/462a44bd90d800e38770d3420e2ca3c7a630b999","verification":{"payload